              "text": "To solve this problem, we need to check if the function \\( f \\) is injective (one-to-one). If \\( f \\) is injective, then for any \\( x \\in S \\), if \\( g(f(x)) = h(f(x)) \\), it must be that \\( g(x) = h(x) \\).\n\nHere's the step-by-step plan:\n1. Read the number of elements \\( N \\) in the set \\( S \\).\n2. Read the elements of the set \\( S \\) and the map \\( f \\).\n3. Check if the map \\( f \\) is injective.\n4. If \\( f \\) is injective, output \"Yes\". Otherwise, provide a counterexample.\n\nLet's implement this in Python:\n\n```python\n# Read the number of elements in the set S\nN = int(input())\n\n# Read the elements of the set S\nS = list(map(int, input().split()))\n\n# Read the map f\nf = list(map(int, input().split()))\n\n# Create a dictionary to map each element in S to its image under f\nf_map = {S[i]: f[i] for i in range(N)}\n\n# Check if the map f is injective\nis_injective = len(set(f)) == N\n\n# If the map is injective, output \"Yes\"\nif is_injective:\n    print(\"Yes\")\nelse:\n    # If the map is not injective, find a counterexample\n    # Find an element x and y such that f(x) = f(y) but x != y\n    for x in S:\n        for y in S:\n            if f_map[x] == f_map[y] and x != y:\n                print(\"No\")\n                print(x, y)\n                break\n        else:\n            continue\n        break\n    else:\n        print(\"Yes\")\n```\n\nThis script will read the input, check if the map \\( f \\) is injective, and output \"Yes\" if it is, or provide a counterexample if it is not.",
