              "length": 539,
              "text": "To solve this problem, we need to verify if the function \\( f \\) is injective (one-to-one). If \\( f \\) is injective, then for any \\( x \\in S \\), if \\( g(f(x)) = h(f(x)) \\), it must be that \\( g(x) = h(x) \\). If \\( f \\) is not injective, we can find a counterexample where \\( g(f(x)) = h(f(x)) \\) but \\( g(x) \\neq h(x) \\).\n\nHere's the Python script to solve the problem:\n\n```python\n# Read the number of elements in the set S\nN = int(input())\n\n# Read the elements of the set S\nS = list(map(int, input().split()))\n\n# Read the mapping f\nf_map = list(map(int, input().split()))\n\n# Create a dictionary to map each element to its image under f\nf_dict = {}\nfor i in range(N):\n    f_dict[S[i]] = f_map[i]\n\n# Check if f is injective\nis_injective = True\nfor i in range(N):\n    for j in range(i + 1, N):\n        if f_dict[S[i]] == f_dict[S[j]]:\n            is_injective = False\n            break\n    if not is_injective:\n        break\n\n# If f is injective, output \"Yes\", otherwise output \"No\"\nif is_injective:\n    print(\"Yes\")\nelse:\n    print(\"No\")\n```\n\nLet's break down the script:\n\n1. **Read the number of elements in the set \\( S \\)**: This is done using `N = int(input())`.\n2. **Read the elements of the set \\( S \\)**: This is done using `S = list(map(int, input().split()))`.\n3. **Read the mapping \\( f \\)**: This is done using `f_map = list(map(int, input().split()))`.\n4. **Create a dictionary to map each element to its image under \\( f \\)**: This is done using a for loop that iterates over the elements of \\( S \\) and populates the dictionary `f_dict`.\n5. **Check if \\( f \\) is injective**: This is done by iterating over the elements of \\( S \\) and checking if any two different elements map to the same element under \\( f \\).\n6. **Output the result**: If \\( f \\) is injective, print \"Yes\", otherwise print \"No\".\n\nThis script will correctly determine if the function \\( f \\) is injective and output the appropriate result.",
