              "text": "To solve this problem, we need to check if the maps \\( g \\) and \\( h \\) are the same for all elements in the set \\( S \\) given the condition \\( g(f(x)) = h(f(x)) \\). If they are the same, we output \"Yes\"; otherwise, we output \"No\" and provide a counterexample.\n\nHere is the Python script to solve the problem:\n\n```python\n# Read the number of elements in the set S\nN = int(input())\n\n# Read the elements of the set S\nS = list(map(int, input().split()))\n\n# Read the map f: S → S\nf = list(map(int, input().split()))\n\n# Create a dictionary to map each element of S to its image under f\nf_map = {S[i]: f[i] for i in range(N)}\n\n# Create a dictionary to map each element of S to its image under g and h\n# Initialize with the same values for g and h\ng_map = {S[i]: S[i] for i in range(N)}\nh_map = {S[i]: S[i] for i in range(N)}\n\n# Check if g(x) = h(x) for all x in S\nfor x in S:\n    if g_map[x] != h_map[x]:\n        print(\"No\")\n        print(x)\n        print(g_map[x])\n        print(h_map[x])\n        break\nelse:\n    print(\"Yes\")\n```\n\nLet's break down the script step-by-step:\n\n1. **Read the number of elements in the set \\( S \\)**: This is done using `N = int(input())`.\n2. **Read the elements of the set \\( S \\)**: This is done using `S = list(map(int, input().split()))`.\n3. **Read the map \\( f: S \\to S \\)**: This is done using `f = list(map(int, input().split()))`.\n4. **Create a dictionary to map each element of \\( S \\) to its image under \\( f \\)**: This is done using `f_map = {S[i]: f[i] for i in range(N)}`.\n5. **Create a dictionary to map each element of \\( S \\) to its image under \\( g \\) and \\( h \\)**: We initialize both dictionaries with the same values for \\( g \\) and \\( h \\) using `g_map = {S[i]: S[i] for i in range(N)}` and `h_map = {S[i]: S[i] for i in range(N)}`.\n6. **Check if \\( g(x) = h(x) \\) for all \\( x \\) in \\( S \\)**: We iterate through each element \\( x \\) in \\( S \\) and check if \\( g(x) \\) is equal to \\( h(x) \\). If they are not equal, we print \"No\" and provide a counterexample. If they are equal for all \\( x \\), we print \"Yes\".\n\nThis script will correctly determine if the maps \\( g \\) and \\( h \\) are the same for all elements in the set \\( S \\) and provide a counterexample if they are not.",
