              "text": "Sure, let's break down the problem and write a Python script to solve it.\n\n### Problem Breakdown\n- We have a set \\( S = \\{a_1, a_2, \\ldots, a_N\\} \\).\n- We have a map \\( f: S \\to S \\) such that \\( f(a_i) = b_i \\).\n- We need to check if for any element \\( x \\) in \\( S \\), all maps \\( g, h: S \\to S \\) satisfying \\( g(f(x)) = h(f(x)) \\) also satisfy \\( g(x) = h(x) \\).\n\n### Steps to Solve\n1. Read the input values \\( N \\) (the size of the set \\( S \\)), and the two sequences \\( a_i \\) and \\( b_i \\).\n2. Check if the function \\( f \\) is injective (one-to-one). If \\( f \\) is not injective, we can find a counterexample.\n3. If \\( f \\) is injective, then for any \\( x \\) in \\( S \\), \\( g(x) = h(x) \\) if \\( g(f(x)) = h(f(x)) \\).\n\n### Python Script\n```python\n# Read input values\nN = int(input())\na = list(map(int, input().split()))\nb = list(map(int, input().split()))\n\n# Create a dictionary to represent the function f\nf = {a[i]: b[i] for i in range(N)}\n\n# Check if f is injective\nis_injective = True\nf_values = set()\nfor key in f:\n    if f[key] in f_values:\n        is_injective = False\n        break\n    f_values.add(f[key])\n\n# Determine the output based on the injectivity of f\nif is_injective:\n    print(\"Yes\")\nelse:\n    print(\"No\")\n```\n\n### Explanation\n- We first read the input values \\( N \\), and the two sequences \\( a \\) and \\( b \\).\n- We then create a dictionary \\( f \\) where the key is an element of \\( S \\) and the value is \\( f(a_i) \\).\n- We check if the function \\( f \\) is injective by verifying if any value in \\( f \\) is repeated.\n- If \\( f \\) is injective, we print \"Yes\". Otherwise, we print \"No\".\n\n### Example\nFor the given example:\n- \\( N = 5 \\)\n- \\( a = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5] \\)\n- \\( b = [3, 4, 2, 5, 1] \\)\n\nThe function \\( f \\) is represented as:\n- \\( f(1) = 3 \\)\n- \\( f(2) = 4 \\)\n- \\( f(3) = 2 \\)\n- \\( f(4) = 5 \\)\n- \\( f(5) = 1 \\)\n\nSince all values in \\( f \\) are unique, the function \\( f \\) is injective, and the output is \"Yes\".",
