              "text": "To solve this problem, we need to simulate the growth and death of a numoeba over time based on the given rules. We will use a tree data structure to represent the numoeba and a stack to process the cells in a top-down manner. Here's the Python script to achieve this:\n\n```python\nimport sys\n\nclass Node:\n    def __init__(self, value):\n        self.value = value\n        self.parent = None\n        self.children = []\n        self.is_leader = False\n\ndef max_odd_factor(n):\n    while n % 2 == 0:\n        n //= 2\n    return n\n\ndef calculate_new_value(n):\n    n = 3 * n + 1\n    max_odd = max_odd_factor(n)\n    if max_odd > 12345678:\n        max_odd -= 12345678\n    return max_odd\n\ndef spawn_child(node, new_value):\n    child = Node(new_value)\n    child.parent = node\n    node.children.append(child)\n\ndef process_node(node):\n    if node.is_leaf and node.value > 1:\n        node.is_leaf = False\n        spawn_child(node, (node.value + 1) // 2)\n    elif node.value == 1:\n        if node.is_leader:\n            return False\n        for child in node.children:\n            if process_node(child):\n                return True\n        return False\n    else:\n        for child in node.children:\n            if process_node(child):\n                return True\n    return False\n\ndef find_new_leader(root):\n    max_value = -1\n    new_leader = None\n    for node in root.children:\n        if node.value > max_value:\n            max_value = node.value\n            new_leader = node\n    if new_leader:\n        new_leader.is_leader = True\n        spawn_child(new_leader, (new_leader.value + 1) // 2)\n        return True\n    return False\n\ndef numoeba_life(seed):\n    root = Node(seed)\n    root.is_leader = True\n    num_cells = 1\n    max_cells = 1\n    for clock in range(1, 500):\n        num_leafs = 0\n        for node in root.children:\n            node.value = calculate_new_value(node.value)\n            if node.value > 1:\n                num_leafs += 1\n            else:\n                if node.is_leader:\n                    return clock, max_cells\n                for child in node.children:\n                    if process_node(child):\n                        return clock, max_cells\n        if num_leafs == 0:\n            break\n        if find_new_leader(root):\n            num_cells += 1\n            max_cells = max(max_cells, num_cells)\n    return clock, max_cells\n\ndef main():\n    for line in sys.stdin:\n        seed = int(line.strip())\n        if seed == 0:\n            break\n        life_time, max_cells = numoeba_life(seed)\n        print(f\"{life_time} {max_cells}\")\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```\n\n### Explanation:\n1. **Node Class**: Represents a cell in the numoeba. It has a value, parent, children, and a boolean to indicate if it is the leader.\n2. **max_odd_factor**: Calculates the maximum odd factor of a number by repeatedly dividing by 2.\n3. **calculate_new_value**: Computes the new numbosome value for a cell.\n4. **spawn_child**: Creates a new child node with a given value.\n5. **process_node**: Processes a node and its children based on the rules for leaf cells and cell death.\n6. **find_new_leader**: Finds the new leader of the numoeba based on the maximum numbosome value.\n7. **numoeba_life**: Simulates the growth and death of the numoeba over time and returns the life time and maximum number of cells.\n8. **main**: Reads the input, processes each seed, and prints the results.\n\nThis script reads the input, processes each seed, and outputs the life time and maximum number of cells for each numoeba.",
