              "text": "To solve this problem, we need to simulate the life of the numoeba based on the given initial numbosome values. We will follow the steps described in the problem statement to determine the life time and the maximum number of constituent cells in the numoeba's life.\n\nHere is the Python script to achieve this:\n\n```python\ndef max_odd_factor(n):\n    while n % 2 == 0:\n        n //= 2\n    return n\n\ndef next_numbosome_value(n):\n    next_val = 3 * n + 1\n    max_factor = max_odd_factor(next_val)\n    if max_factor > 12345678:\n        max_factor -= 12345678\n    return max_factor\n\ndef calculate_fate(numoeba, root):\n    candidate_leaves = []\n    to_die = []\n    for cell in numoeba:\n        if cell['numbosome'] > 1:\n            cell['numbosome'] = next_numbosome_value(cell['numbosome'])\n        if cell['numbosome'] == 1:\n            to_die.append(cell)\n        elif cell['is_leaf'] and cell['numbosome'] > 1:\n            candidate_leaves.append(cell)\n    \n    for cell in to_die:\n        if cell['is_leader']:\n            numoeba.remove(cell)\n            return 0, len(numoeba)\n        else:\n            subtree = [cell]\n            parent = cell['parent']\n            while parent and parent['numbosome'] != 1:\n                subtree.append(parent)\n                parent = parent['parent']\n            numoeba.remove(cell)\n            for c in subtree:\n                numoeba.remove(c)\n            if len(subtree) > 1 or (len(subtree) == 1 and subtree[0]['numbosome'] == 1):\n                return 0, len(numoeba)\n            else:\n                cell['parent']['children'].remove(cell)\n                cell['parent']['children'].append(subtree[0])\n                subtree[0]['parent'] = cell['parent']\n    \n    for leaf in candidate_leaves:\n        new_leaf = {'numbosome': (leaf['numbosome'] + 1) // 2, 'parent': leaf['parent']}\n        leaf['parent']['children'].append(new_leaf)\n        new_leaf['parent'] = leaf['parent']\n    \n    max_numbosome = max(cell['numbosome'] for cell in numoeba)\n    for cell in numoeba:\n        if cell['numbosome'] == max_numbosome:\n            new_leader = {'numbosome': (max_numbosome + 1) // 2, 'parent': cell['parent']}\n            cell['parent']['children'].append(new_leader)\n            new_leader['parent'] = cell['parent']\n            return 1, len(numoeba)\n    return 1, len(numoeba)\n\ndef simulate_numoeba(start_value):\n    numoeba = [{'numbosome': start_value, 'parent': None, 'children': [], 'is_leaf': True, 'is_leader': True}]\n    clock = 0\n    max_cells = 1\n    while True:\n        clock += 1\n        status, cells = calculate_fate(numoeba, numoeba[0])\n        if status == 0:\n            return clock, max_cells\n        max_cells = max(max_cells, cells)\n\ndef main():\n    while True:\n        start_value = int(input())\n        if start_value == 0:\n            break\n        lifetime, max_cells = simulate_numoeba(start_value)\n        print(f\"{lifetime} {max_cells}\")\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```\n\nThis script defines the necessary functions to simulate the life of the numoeba and calculates the lifetime and the maximum number of constituent cells. It reads the input, processes it, and outputs the required statistics.",
