              "text": "To solve this problem, we need to simulate the growth and death of numoebae based on the given rules. We will use a tree structure to represent the numoeba, and we will update the numbosome values and check the conditions at each clock.\n\nLet's break down the steps:\n\n1. **Read the initial numbosome value**.\n2. **Initialize the numoeba tree**.\n3. **Simulate each clock**:\n   - Calculate the new numbosome values.\n   - Determine the fate of each cell.\n   - Update the tree structure.\n4. **Output the results**.\n\nHere is the Python script to achieve this:\n\n```python\nclass Numoeba:\n    def __init__(self, root_value):\n        self.root = Node(root_value)\n        self.current_clock = 0\n        self.max_cells = 1  # Start with the root node\n\n    def update_numbo_value(self, node):\n        new_value = (3 * node.value + 1)\n        while new_value % 2 == 0:\n            new_value //= 2\n        if new_value > 12345678:\n            new_value -= 12345678\n        node.value = new_value\n\n    def update_fate(self, node):\n        if node.is_leaf() and node.value > 1:\n            node.is_candidate_leaf = True\n        if node.value == 1:\n            if node == self.root:\n                self.die()\n            else:\n                node.parent.remove_child(node)\n                if len(node.parent.children) == 1:\n                    node.parent.children[0].parent = node.parent.parent\n                    node.parent.parent.children.remove(node.parent)\n                    node.parent.parent.children.append(node.parent.children[0])\n        if node.is_candidate_leaf:\n            node.value = (node.value + 1) // 2\n            if node.value % 2 != 0:\n                bonus_child = Node(node.value)\n                bonus_child.parent = node\n                node.children.append(bonus_child)\n                self.max_cells += 1\n\n    def update_leader(self):\n        max_value = 0\n        new_leader = None\n        for node in self.all_nodes():\n            if node.value > max_value:\n                max_value = node.value\n                new_leader = node\n        if new_leader:\n            self.root = new_leader\n            self.update_numbo_value(new_leader)\n            if new_leader.value % 2 != 0:\n                bonus_child = Node((new_leader.value + 1) // 2)\n                bonus_child.parent = new_leader\n                new_leader.children.append(bonus_child)\n                self.max_cells += 1\n\n    def die(self):\n        self.root.value = 1\n        self.max_cells = 0\n\n    def all_nodes(self):\n        nodes = [self.root]\n        for node in self.root.children:\n            nodes.extend(node.all_nodes())\n        return nodes\n\n    def simulate_clock(self):\n        self.current_clock += 1\n        for node in self.all_nodes():\n            self.update_numbo_value(node)\n            self.update_fate(node)\n        self.update_leader()\n\n    def run_simulation(self):\n        while self.current_clock < 500:\n            self.simulate_clock()\n            if self.root.value == 1:\n                break\n            self.max_cells = max(self.max_cells, len(self.all_nodes()))\n        return self.current_clock, self.max_cells\n\nclass Node:\n    def __init__(self, value):\n        self.value = value\n        self.children = []\n        self.parent = None\n        self.is_candidate_leaf = False\n\n    def is_leaf(self):\n        return not self.children\n\n    def remove_child(self, child):\n        self.children.remove(child)\n\n    def all_nodes(self):\n        nodes = [self]\n        for child in self.children:\n            nodes.extend(child.all_nodes())\n        return nodes\n\ndef main():\n    while True:\n        try:\n            initial_value = int(input())\n            if initial_value == 0:\n                break\n            numoeba = Numoeba(initial_value)\n            lifetime, max_cells = numoeba.run_simulation()\n            print(lifetime, max_cells)\n        except EOFError:\n            break\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```\n\nThis script defines a `Numoeba` class to simulate the growth and death of numoebae, and a `Node` class to represent the cells in the tree. The `main` function reads the initial numbosome values and runs the simulation for each value, outputting the lifetime and maximum number of cells.",
