              "text": "To solve this problem, we need to simulate the growth and death of the numoeba over time. We will follow the steps described in the problem statement to update the numbosome values, identify candidate leaves, and determine the fate of the cells. We will also keep track of the maximum number of cells and the life time of the numoeba.\n\nHere's a Python script that accomplishes this:\n\n```python\ndef get_max_odd_factor(n):\n    while n % 2 == 0:\n        n //= 2\n    return n\n\ndef update_numbosome_value(n):\n    n = 3 * n + 1\n    max_odd_factor = get_max_odd_factor(n)\n    if max_odd_factor > 12345678:\n        max_odd_factor -= 12345678\n    return max_odd_factor\n\ndef is_cell_dead(n):\n    return n == 1\n\ndef get_new_leaf_value(n):\n    return (n + 1) // 2\n\ndef get_new_leader_value(n):\n    return (n + 1) // 2\n\ndef process_numoeba(seed):\n    numoeba = [{'value': seed, 'children': [], 'parent': None, 'is_dead': False}]\n\n    max_cells = 1\n    max_lifetime = 0\n\n    for clock in range(1, 500):\n        new_numoeba = []\n        max_value = 0\n        for cell in numoeba:\n            if not cell['is_dead']:\n                cell['value'] = update_numbosome_value(cell['value'])\n                if is_cell_dead(cell['value']):\n                    cell['is_dead'] = True\n                    if cell['value'] == seed:\n                        return clock, max_cells\n                else:\n                    if cell['value'] > max_value:\n                        max_value = cell['value']\n                    new_leaf_value = get_new_leaf_value(cell['value'])\n                    new_leader_value = get_new_leader_value(cell['value'])\n                    new_numoeba.append({'value': cell['value'], 'children': [], 'parent': cell, 'is_dead': False})\n                    if new_leaf_value > max_value:\n                        max_value = new_leaf_value\n                    if new_leader_value > max_value:\n                        max_value = new_leader_value\n\n                    if cell['value'] > max_value:\n                        max_value = cell['value']\n                    new_numoeba.append({'value': new_leaf_value, 'children': [], 'parent': cell, 'is_dead': False})\n                    new_numoeba.append({'value': new_leader_value, 'children': [], 'parent': cell, 'is_dead': False})\n\n        numoeba = new_numoeba\n        if len(numoeba) > max_cells:\n            max_cells = len(numoeba)\n\n    return max_lifetime, max_cells\n\ndef main():\n    while True:\n        try:\n            seed = int(input())\n            if seed == 0:\n                break\n            lifetime, max_cells = process_numoeba(seed)\n            print(f\"{lifetime} {max_cells}\")\n        except EOFError:\n            break\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```\n\nThis script defines the necessary functions to update the numbosome values, check if a cell is dead, and generate new leaf and leader values. It then processes the numoeba over time, updating the structure and counting the maximum number of cells and the lifetime of the numoeba. The main function reads the input, processes each seed value, and prints the results.",
