              "text": "To solve this problem, we need to simulate the behavior of the numoeba over time. We will use a tree structure to represent the numoeba and update the numbosome values of the cells at each biological clock. We will also keep track of the leader and the number of cells in the numoeba.\n\nHere is the Python script to solve the problem:\n\n```python\nclass Node:\n    def __init__(self, value):\n        self.value = value\n        self.parent = None\n        self.children = []\n        self.is_leaf = True\n\ndef get_max_odd_factor(n):\n    while n % 2 == 0:\n        n //= 2\n    return n\n\ndef update_numbosome(node):\n    new_value = get_max_odd_factor(3 * node.value + 1)\n    if new_value > 12345678:\n        new_value -= 12345678\n    node.value = new_value\n\ndef is_leaf(node):\n    return len(node.children) == 0\n\ndef update_numoeba(numoeba):\n    # Step 1: Identify candidate leaves\n    candidate_leaves = [node for node in numoeba if is_leaf(node) and node.value > 1]\n\n    # Step 2: Determine cell deaths\n    for node in candidate_leaves:\n        if node.value == 1:\n            if node == numoeba[0]:\n                return False, 0\n            else:\n                numoeba.remove(node)\n                for child in node.children:\n                    child.parent = node.parent\n                    node.parent.children.append(child)\n                if len(node.parent.children) == 1:\n                    node.parent.children[0].parent = node.parent.parent\n                    if node.parent.parent:\n                        node.parent.parent.children.remove(node.parent)\n                        node.parent.parent.children.append(node.parent.children[0])\n                    else:\n                        numoeba[0] = node.parent.children[0]\n                        node.parent.children[0].parent = numoeba[0]\n                return True, len(numoeba)\n\n    # Step 3: Create bonus leaves\n    for node in candidate_leaves:\n        new_value = (node.value + 1) // 2\n        new_leaf = Node(new_value)\n        new_leaf.parent = node\n        node.children.append(new_leaf)\n        new_leaf.is_leaf = True\n\n    # Step 4: Determine new leader\n    max_value = max(node.value for node in numoeba)\n    new_leader = [node for node in numoeba if node.value == max_value][0]\n    new_leader.is_leaf = False\n    numoeba.remove(new_leader)\n    new_leader.children = [node for node in numoeba if node.parent == new_leader]\n    new_leader.parent = None\n    numoeba.insert(0, new_leader)\n    new_leader.children[0].parent = new_leader\n\n    # Step 5: Create bonus leader\n    new_leader.value = (max_value + 1) // 2\n    new_leader.children.append(Node(new_leader.value))\n    new_leader.children[0].parent = new_leader\n\n    return True, len(numoeba)\n\ndef main():\n    while True:\n        try:\n            k = int(input())\n            if k == 0:\n                break\n            numoeba = [Node(k)]\n            max_cells = 1\n            max_time = 1\n            while True:\n                alive, num_cells = update_numoeba(numoeba)\n                if not alive:\n                    print(max_time, max_cells)\n                    break\n                max_cells = max(max_cells, num_cells)\n                max_time += 1\n        except EOFError:\n            break\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```\n\nThis script defines a `Node` class to represent each cell in the numoeba, and a `main` function to process the input and simulate the numoeba's behavior over time. The `update_numoeba` function handles the logic for updating the numoeba at each biological clock.",
