              "text": "To solve this problem, we need to simulate the life of a numoeba, starting from a single cell with an initial numbosome value. We will follow the rules provided to update the numbosome values, determine the fate of cells, and update the numoeba's structure accordingly. Let's break down the steps and write the Python script.\n\n### Steps to Solve the Problem:\n1. **Read the initial numbosome values** from the input.\n2. **Simulate the life of the numoeba** at each biological clock.\n3. **Track the maximum number of cells** and the lifetime of the numoeba.\n4. **Output the results** for each initial numbosome value.\n\n### Python Script:\n```python\ndef get_max_odd_factor(n):\n    while n % 2 == 0:\n        n //= 2\n    return n\n\ndef update_numbosome(n):\n    n = 3 * n + 1\n    while n % 2 == 0:\n        n //= 2\n    if n > 12345678:\n        n -= 12345678\n    return n\n\ndef is_leaf(node, tree):\n    return len(tree[node]) == 1\n\ndef find_new_leader(tree, current_leader, current_max_numbosome):\n    max_numbosome = current_max_numbosome\n    new_leader = current_leader\n    for node in tree:\n        if node != current_leader:\n            if tree[node] and tree[node][0] != current_leader:\n                numbosome = tree[node][0]\n                if numbosome > max_numbosome:\n                    max_numbosome = numbosome\n                    new_leader = node\n    return new_leader, max_numbosome\n\ndef update_tree(tree, node, current_max_numbosome):\n    if node in tree and tree[node] and tree[node][0] != current_leader:\n        numbosome = tree[node][0]\n        if numbosome == 1:\n            if node == current_leader:\n                return None\n            else:\n                return tree[node][1] if tree[node][1] else None\n        elif is_leaf(node, tree):\n            if numbosome > current_max_numbosome:\n                return None\n            else:\n                child_leaf = (numbosome + 1) // 2\n                tree[node].append(child_leaf)\n                return node\n        else:\n            new_leader, max_numbosome = find_new_leader(tree, node, current_max_numbosome)\n            if new_leader != node:\n                tree[new_leader].append(node)\n                tree[node] = []\n                tree[node] = [max_numbosome]\n                tree[new_leader].append(max_numbosome)\n                return new_leader\n            else:\n                child_leaf = (numbosome + 1) // 2\n                tree[node].append(child_leaf)\n                return node\n\ndef simulate_numoeba(initial_numbosome):\n    tree = {0: [initial_numbosome]}\n    current_leader = 0\n    current_max_numbosome = initial_numbosome\n    num_cells = 1\n    numoeba_life = 0\n    \n    while True:\n        numoeba_life += 1\n        new_tree = {}\n        for node in tree:\n            if tree[node]:\n                numbosome = tree[node][0]\n                new_numbosome = update_numbosome(numbosome)\n                new_tree[node] = [new_numbosome]\n                if node == current_leader:\n                    current_leader = node\n                    current_max_numbosome = new_numbosome\n                else:\n                    new_leader, max_numbosome = find_new_leader(tree, node, current_max_numbosome)\n                    if new_leader != node:\n                        new_tree[new_leader].append(node)\n                        new_tree[node] = []\n                        new_tree[node] = [max_numbosome]\n                        current_leader = new_leader\n                        current_max_numbosome = max_numbosome\n                    else:\n                        current_max_numbosome = max(current_max_numbosome, new_numbosome)\n        \n        if current_max_numbosome == 1:\n            if current_leader == 0:\n                return numoeba_life, num_cells\n            else:\n                num_cells -= 1\n                for node in tree:\n                    if tree[node] and tree[node][0] == current_leader:\n                        tree[node] = []\n                        tree[node] = [current_max_numbosome]\n                        current_leader = node\n                        current_max_numbosome = new_numbosome\n                        break\n        else:\n            num_cells += 1\n            for node in tree:\n                if tree[node]:\n                    numbosome = tree[node][0]\n                    if numbosome > current_max_numbosome:\n                        current_max_numbosome = numbosome\n                        current_leader = node\n                    else:\n                        child_leaf = (numbosome + 1) // 2\n                        tree[node].append(child_leaf)\n        \n        tree = new_tree\n\n    return numoeba_life, num_cells\n\n# Read input\nwhile True:\n    try:\n        initial_numbosome = int(input())\n        if initial_numbosome == 0:\n            break\n        life_time, max_cells = simulate_numoeba(initial_numbosome)\n        print(life_time, max_cells)\n    except EOFError:\n        break\n```\n\n### Explanation:\n1. **get_max_odd_factor(n)**: This function calculates the maximum odd factor of a number by repeatedly dividing by 2.\n2. **update_numbosome(n)**: This function updates the numbosome value according to the rules provided.\n3. **is_leaf(node, tree)**: This function checks if a node is a leaf.\n4. **find_new_leader(tree, current_leader, current_max_numbosome)**: This function finds the new leader of the numoeba.\n5. **update_tree(tree, node, current_max_numbosome)**: This function updates the tree structure and the leader of the numoeba.\n6. **simulate_numoeba(initial_numbosome)**: This function simulates the life of the numoeba starting from the initial numbosome value and returns the life time and maximum number of cells.\n\nThe script reads the initial numbosome values from the input, simulates the life of the numoeba, and outputs the life time and maximum number of cells for each initial numbosome value.",
