              "text": "To solve the problem of simulating the life of a numoeba, we need to follow the steps described in the problem statement. Here is a step-by-step plan for the Python script:\n\n1. **Tree Representation**: Represent the numoeba as a tree where each node has a numbosome value.\n2. **Biological Clock Simulation**: At each clock, update the numbosome values, determine the fate of the cells, and adjust the tree structure accordingly.\n3. **Output Statistics**: After each clock, calculate and print the lifetime and the maximum number of constituent cells.\n\nHere is the Python script implementing the described steps:\n\n```python\nimport sys\n\nclass Node:\n    def __init__(self, value):\n        self.value = value\n        self.children = []\n        self.parent = None\n\ndef get_max_odd_factor(n):\n    while n % 2 == 0:\n        n //= 2\n    return n\n\ndef update_numbosome(node):\n    value = 3 * node.value + 1\n    factor = get_max_odd_factor(value)\n    new_value = factor if factor <= 12345678 else factor - 12345678\n    node.value = new_value\n    if node.value == 1:\n        return False\n    return True\n\ndef update_numoeba(numoeba):\n    root = numoeba[0]\n    max_value = root.value\n    candidates = []\n    deaths = []\n    \n    def update(node):\n        nonlocal max_value, candidates, deaths\n        if node.value > max_value:\n            max_value = node.value\n        if not node.children:\n            candidates.append(node)\n        else:\n            for child in node.children:\n                update(child)\n        if node.value > 1:\n            if node not in deaths and node.value != 1:\n                deaths.append(node)\n            for child in node.children:\n                if child.value > 1:\n                    deaths.append(child)\n    \n    update(root)\n    \n    # Determine the fate of each candidate leaf\n    for leaf in candidates:\n        new_value = (leaf.value + 1) // 2\n        while new_value % 2 == 0:\n            new_value //= 2\n        new_leaf = Node(new_value)\n        leaf.children.append(new_leaf)\n    \n    # Handle deaths\n    for node in deaths:\n        if node == root:\n            return None\n        parent = node.parent\n        for child in node.children:\n            parent.children.remove(node)\n            parent.children.append(child)\n            child.parent = parent\n            if parent.value == node.value:\n                parent.value = child.value\n        if len(node.children) == 1:\n            child = node.children[0]\n            parent.children.remove(node)\n            parent.children.append(child)\n            child.parent = parent\n        else:\n            deaths.remove(node)\n    \n    return root\n\ndef print_numoeba(numoeba):\n    max_value = 0\n    for node in numoeba:\n        if node.value > max_value:\n            max_value = node.value\n    print(max_value, len(numoeba))\n    return max_value, len(numoeba)\n\ndef main():\n    while True:\n        line = sys.stdin.readline().strip()\n        if line == '0':\n            break\n        numoeba = [Node(int(line))]\n        max_time = 0\n        max_cells = 0\n        \n        for t in range(1, 500):\n            root = update_numoeba(numoeba)\n            if root is None:\n                break\n            max_time = t\n            if t % 10 == 0:\n                max_value, cells = print_numoeba(numoeba)\n                if cells > max_cells:\n                    max_cells = cells\n            numoeba = [root]\n            if not root.children:\n                break\n            for child in root.children:\n                numoeba.append(child)\n        print(f\"{max_time} {max_cells}\")\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```\n\n### Explanation:\n- **Node Class**: Represents a cell in the numoeba tree with its value and children.\n- **get_max_odd_factor**: Computes the maximum odd factor of a given number.\n- **update_numbosome**: Updates the numbosome value of a cell.\n- **update_numoeba**: Simulates the biological clock for the numoeba, updating values, handling deaths, and adjusting the tree structure.\n- **print_numoeba**: Prints the maximum numbosome value and the number of cells in the current state of the numoeba.\n- **main**: Reads the input, simulates the life of the numoeba, and prints the required statistics.\n\nThis script reads the initial numbosome values, simulates the life of the numoeba, and prints the required statistics after each clock.",
