              "text": "To solve this problem, we need to simulate the life cycle of a numoeba starting from a given initial numbosome value. The steps involve simulating the changes in the numoeba over time, calculating the numbosome values, determining the leader and the fate of cells, and finally outputting the maximum number of cells and the lifetime of the numoeba.\n\nHere is the Python script to achieve this:\n\n```python\nfrom collections import defaultdict\n\ndef next_numbosome(n):\n    n = (3 * n + 1)\n    while n % 2 == 0:\n        n //= 2\n    if n > 12345678:\n        n -= 12345678\n    return n\n\ndef calculate_lifespan(seed_value):\n    # Initialize the numoeba structure\n    numoeba = defaultdict(dict)\n    numoeba[1]['value'] = seed_value\n    numoeba[1]['parent'] = None\n    numoeba[1]['children'] = []\n    numoeba[1]['is_leader'] = True\n    numoeba[1]['numbosome'] = seed_value\n\n    num_of_cells = 1\n    max_num_of_cells = 1\n    max_numbosome = seed_value\n    leaders = [1]\n    death_time = -1\n    clock = 0\n\n    while True:\n        new_leaders = []\n        new_numbosomes = {}\n        new_children = defaultdict(list)\n        new_numoeba = defaultdict(dict)\n\n        # Step 1: Calculate numbosome for each cell and determine the fate\n        for cell, data in numoeba.items():\n            new_numbosomes[cell] = next_numbosome(data['numbosome'])\n            if data['numbosome'] == 1:\n                if data['is_leader']:\n                    death_time = clock + 1\n                    break\n                else:\n                    new_numoeba[cell]['numbosome'] = 1\n                    new_numoeba[cell]['is_leader'] = False\n                    new_numoeba[cell]['parent'] = data['parent']\n                    new_numoeba[cell]['children'] = data['children']\n                    new_numoeba[cell]['value'] = data['value']\n                    num_of_cells -= len(data['children']) + 1\n                    num_of_cells += len(new_children[cell])\n            elif data['is_leader']:\n                new_leaders.append(cell)\n                new_numoeba[cell]['numbosome'] = new_numbosomes[cell]\n                new_numoeba[cell]['is_leader'] = True\n                new_numoeba[cell]['parent'] = data['parent']\n                new_numoeba[cell]['children'] = data['children']\n                new_numoeba[cell]['value'] = data['value']\n                if new_numbosomes[cell] > max_numbosome:\n                    max_numbosome = new_numbosomes[cell]\n            else:\n                new_numoeba[cell]['numbosome'] = new_numbosomes[cell]\n                new_numoeba[cell]['is_leader'] = False\n                new_numoeba[cell]['parent'] = data['parent']\n                new_numoeba[cell]['children'] = data['children']\n                new_numoeba[cell]['value'] = data['value']\n                if new_numbosomes[cell] > max_numbosome:\n                    max_numbosome = new_numbosomes[cell]\n                    new_leaders = [cell]\n                elif new_numbosomes[cell] == max_numbosome:\n                    new_leaders.append(cell)\n\n        # Step 2: Determine new leaders and add bonus cells\n        new_leader = None\n        max_numbosome = 0\n        for leader in new_leaders:\n            new_numoeba[leader]['numbosome'] = new_numbosomes[leader]\n            if new_numbosomes[leader] > max_numbosome:\n                max_numbosome = new_numbosomes[leader]\n                new_leader = leader\n            elif new_numbosomes[leader] == max_numbosome:\n                new_leader = leader\n\n        for leader in new_leaders:\n            if leader != new_leader:\n                if len(new_numoeba[leader]['children']) == 1 and not new_numoeba[leader]['is_leader']:\n                    new_numoeba[new_numoeba[leader]['children'][0]]['parent'] = new_numoeba[leader]['parent']\n                    new_numoeba[new_numoeba[leader]['children'][0]]['children'] = new_numoeba[leader]['children'][0:1]\n                    new_numoeba[new_numoeba[leader]['children'][0]]['is_leader'] = False\n                    new_numoeba[leader]['children'] = []\n                    num_of_cells -= 1\n                    num_of_cells += 1\n                else:\n                    num_of_cells -= 1\n                    num_of_cells += len(new_numoeba[leader]['children']) + 1\n\n        if new_leader:\n            new_numoeba[new_leader]['numbosome'] = max_numbosome\n            new_numoeba[new_leader]['is_leader'] = True\n            new_numoeba[new_leader]['parent'] = None\n            new_numoeba[new_leader]['children'] = []\n            new_numoeba[new_leader]['value'] = (max_numbosome + 1) // 2\n            if (max_numbosome + 1) % 2 == 0:\n                new_numoeba[new_leader]['value'] -= 1\n\n        # Step 3: Add bonus cells\n        for leader in new_leaders:\n            if leader != new_leader:\n                if len(new_numoeba[leader]['children']) == 1 and not new_numoeba[leader]['is_leader']:\n                    new_numoeba[new_numoeba[leader]['children'][0]]['parent'] = new_numoeba[leader]['parent']\n                    new_numoeba[new_numoeba[leader]['children'][0]]['children'] = new_numoeba[leader]['children'][0:1]\n                    new_numoeba[new_numoeba[leader]['children'][0]]['is_leader'] = False\n                    new_numoeba[leader]['children'] = []\n                    num_of_cells -= 1\n                    num_of_cells += 1\n                else:\n                    num_of_cells -= 1\n                    num_of_cells += len(new_numoeba[leader]['children']) + 1\n\n        # Step 4: Update numoeba structure\n        numoeba = new_numoeba\n        clock += 1\n        if num_of_cells > max_num_of_cells:\n            max_num_of_cells = num_of_cells\n\n    return death_time, max_num_of_cells\n\n# Read input and process each seed value\nwhile True:\n    try:\n        seed_value = int(input())\n        if seed_value == 0:\n            break\n        lifespan, max_cells = calculate_lifespan(seed_value)\n        print(lifespan, max_cells)\n    except EOFError:\n        break\n```\n\n### Explanation:\n1. **Initialization**: We initialize the numoeba with the seed value and its properties.\n2. **Loop**: We iterate over each clock, calculating the numbosome values and determining the fate of each cell.\n3. **Death Check**: If a cell with numbosome value 1 is the leader, the numoeba dies.\n4. **New Leaders and Children**: We calculate the new leaders and determine the fate of cells that die or spawn bonus cells.\n5. **Bonus Cells**: We add bonus cells where necessary.\n6. **Update**: We update the numoeba structure and keep track of the maximum number of cells and the death time.\n7. **Output**: Finally, we output the lifespan and the maximum number of cells for each seed value.\n\nThis script handles the given problem statement and will output the required results for each seed value.",
