              "text": "To solve the problem, we need to simulate the life of a numoeba starting from a given initial numbosome value. We will follow these steps:\n\n1. **Input Handling**: Read the initial numbosome values.\n2. **Structure Representation**: Represent the numoeba as a tree structure.\n3. **Simulate Clocks**: Simulate the changes in numbosome values and determine the fate of the cells.\n4. **Output Statistics**: Calculate and output the lifetime and maximum number of cells for each numoeba.\n\nHere is the Python script to achieve this:\n\n```python\nimport sys\n\ndef max_odd_factor(n):\n    while n % 2 == 0:\n        n //= 2\n    return n\n\ndef process_numoeba(numbosome, parent=None, depth=0):\n    if numbosome == 1:\n        return [], 1  # Cell dies, no more children\n    \n    children = []\n    new_numbosome = max_odd_factor(3 * numbosome + 1)\n    if new_numbosome > 12345678:\n        new_numbosome -= 12345678\n    \n    if new_numbosome != 1:\n        children.append(process_numoeba(new_numbosome, parent, depth + 1))\n    \n    return children, (depth + 1)\n\ndef simulate_numoeba(initial_numbosome):\n    tree = {}\n    root = (initial_numbosome, None)\n    tree[root[0]] = root\n    \n    for clock in range(1, 500):  # Simulate up to 500 clocks\n        new_tree = {}\n        candidates = []\n        max_numbosome = -1\n        for cell, parent in tree.items():\n            if parent is not None:\n                parent_numbosome, _ = parent\n                if cell not in tree and max_odd_factor(3 * cell + 1) > 1:\n                    # Calculate new numbosome and check if it's a candidate leaf\n                    new_numbosome = max_odd_factor(3 * cell + 1)\n                    if new_numbosome > 12345678:\n                        new_numbosome -= 12345678\n                    if new_numbosome > parent_numbosome:\n                        candidates.append(cell)\n            else:\n                # Check if it's a candidate leaf\n                new_numbosome = (cell + 1) // 2\n                while new_numbosome % 2 == 0:\n                    new_numbosome //= 2\n                candidates.append(cell)\n            \n            # Determine the new numbosome value\n            new_numbosome = max_odd_factor(3 * cell + 1)\n            if new_numbosome > 12345678:\n                new_numbosome -= 12345678\n            \n            if new_numbosome != 1:\n                # Create a child cell\n                new_cell = (new_numbosome, cell)\n                new_tree[new_cell[0]] = new_cell\n                candidates.append(new_cell[0])\n            else:\n                # Cell dies, remove from tree\n                del new_tree[cell]\n        \n        # Update the tree structure\n        tree = new_tree\n        \n        # Determine the new leader and bonus\n        max_numbosome = max(tree.keys())\n        new_leader = (max_numbosome, None)\n        if len(tree) > 1:\n            new_leader = max(tree.items(), key=lambda x: x[0])\n        \n        # Create leader bonus\n        leader_bonus = (max_numbosome + 1) // 2\n        while leader_bonus % 2 == 0:\n            leader_bonus //= 2\n        new_tree[leader_bonus] = (leader_bonus, new_leader[0])\n        \n        # Check if the leader dies\n        if max_numbosome == 1:\n            return clock, len(tree)\n        \n        # Update the tree with the new leader\n        tree[new_leader[0]] = new_leader\n    \n    return 500, len(tree)\n\n# Read input\ninput_data = sys.stdin.readlines()\ninput_data = [int(line.strip()) for line in input_data if line.strip()]\n\n# Process each initial numbosome value\nfor num in input_data:\n    if num == 0:\n        break\n    lifetime, max_cells = simulate_numoeba(num)\n    print(f\"{lifetime} {max_cells}\")\n```\n\n### Explanation:\n1. **Function `max_odd_factor(n)`**: This function calculates the maximum odd factor of a given number.\n2. **Function `process_numoeba(numbosome, parent=None, depth=0)`**: This function simulates the growth and death of a numoeba starting from a single cell. It recursively processes each cell and updates the tree structure.\n3. **Function `simulate_numoeba(initial_numbosome)`**: This function simulates the life of the numoeba for up to 500 clocks. It keeps track of the tree structure and calculates the maximum numbosome value, which determines the new leader and bonus cells.\n4. **Main Loop**: The script reads the input, processes each initial numbosome value, and prints the lifetime and maximum number of cells for each numoeba.\n\nThis script should handle the given problem constraints and provide the required output.",
