              "text": "Certainly! Let's write a Python script to solve this problem. The script will read an input sentence, split it into words based on the specified delimiters, and then filter the words to only include those with 3 to 6 letters. Finally, it will output the filtered words separated by a single space.\n\nHere is the Python script:\n\n```python\n# Read input from the user\nsentence = input().strip()\n\n# Define the delimiters\ndelimiters = \" .,\"\n\n# Split the sentence into words using the delimiters\nwords = []\nfor char in sentence:\n    if char in delimiters:\n        continue\n    elif char.isalpha():\n        words[-1] += char\n    else:\n        words.append('')\n\n# Filter words to only include those with 3 to 6 letters\nfiltered_words = [word for word in words if 2 < len(word) < 7]\n\n# Join the filtered words with a single space\noutput = ' '.join(filtered_words)\n\n# Print the result\nprint(output)\n```\n\nThis script will process the input sentence, filter the words based on the specified criteria, and then output the result.",
