              "text": "Certainly! Here's a Python script that processes the input sentence and extracts words with 3 to 6 letters, separated by a single space.\n\n```python\n# Read input from the user\ninput_sentence = input().strip()\n\n# Define the delimiters\ndelimiters = [' ', ',', '.', '!', '?']\n\n# Split the sentence into words using the delimiters\nwords = []\ncurrent_word = ''\nfor char in input_sentence:\n    if char in delimiters:\n        if 3 <= len(current_word) <= 6:\n            words.append(current_word)\n        current_word = ''\n    else:\n        current_word += char\n\n# Add the last word if it's within the specified length\nif 3 <= len(current_word) <= 6:\n    words.append(current_word)\n\n# Join the words with a single space and print the result\nprint(' '.join(words))\n```\n\nThis script reads the input sentence, splits it into words using the specified delimiters, and then filters out words with 3 to 6 letters. Finally, it prints the filtered words separated by a single space.",
