              "text": "```python\nwhile True:\n    # Read the number of destinations\n    N = int(input())\n    if N == 0:\n        break\n\n    # Read the coordinates of the non-poisonous land rectangle\n    A, B, C, D = map(int, input().split())\n\n    # Read the initial coordinates of the character\n    X0, Y0 = map(int, input().split())\n\n    # Read the coordinates of the N destinations\n    destinations = [tuple(map(int, input().split())) for _ in range(N)]\n\n    # Function to calculate the Manhattan distance\n    def manhattan_distance(x1, y1, x2, y2):\n        return abs(x1 - x2) + abs(y1 - y2)\n\n    # Function to check if a cell is a non-poisonous land\n    def is_non_poisonous_land(x, y):\n        return A <= x <= C and B <= y <= D\n\n    # Function to calculate the damage\n    def calculate_damage(start_x, start_y, end_x, end_y):\n        # Calculate the distance via the non-poisonous land rectangle\n        damage = 0\n        for x in range(min(start_x, end_x), max(start_x, end_x) + 1):\n            for y in range(min(start_y, end_y), max(start_y, end_y) + 1):\n                if is_non_poisonous_land(x, y):\n                    damage += 1\n        return damage\n\n    # Calculate the damage for each destination\n    total_damage = 0\n    current_x, current_y = X0, Y0\n    for destination in destinations:\n        x, y = destination\n        # Calculate the damage for the current move\n        if not is_non_poisonous_land(current_x, current_y):\n            total_damage += 1\n        # Calculate the damage for the move to the destination\n        damage_to_destination = calculate_damage(current_x, current_y, x, y)\n        total_damage += damage_to_destination\n        # Update the current position\n        current_x, current_y = x, y\n\n    print(total_damage)\n```\n\nThis script reads the input, processes each dataset, and calculates the number of times the character will be damaged by moving to each destination, taking into account the non-poisonous land rectangle.",
