              "text": "To solve this problem, we need to determine the number of times the character will be damaged when visiting N destinations in sequence, minimizing the number of times the character is damaged by choosing the right route. We will use the provided coordinates and the range of the non-poisonous land to calculate the damage.\n\nHere is the Python script to solve the problem:\n\n```python\nwhile True:\n    # Read the number of destinations N\n    N = int(input())\n    if N == 0:\n        break\n\n    # Read the coordinates of the non-poisonous land rectangle\n    A, B, C, D = map(int, input().split())\n\n    # Read the starting coordinates of the character\n    X0, Y0 = map(int, input().split())\n\n    # Read the coordinates of the N destinations\n    destinations = [tuple(map(int, input().split())) for _ in range(N)]\n\n    # Function to calculate the distance between two points\n    def distance(x1, y1, x2, y2):\n        return abs(x1 - x2) + abs(y1 - y2)\n\n    # Function to check if a point is in the non-poisonous land\n    def is_non_poisonous(x, y):\n        return A <= x <= C and B <= y <= D\n\n    # Initialize the number of damages\n    damages = 0\n\n    # Function to calculate the minimum damage\n    def min_damage(X0, Y0, destinations):\n        nonlocal damages\n        for i in range(len(destinations)):\n            for j in range(i + 1, len(destinations)):\n                # Calculate the distance between two destinations\n                dist = distance(destinations[i][0], destinations[i][1], destinations[j][0], destinations[j][1])\n                # Calculate the distance from the start to the first destination\n                dist1 = distance(X0, Y0, destinations[i][0], destinations[i][1])\n                # Calculate the distance from the first destination to the second destination\n                dist2 = distance(destinations[i][0], destinations[i][1], destinations[j][0], destinations[j][1])\n                # Calculate the distance from the second destination back to the start\n                dist3 = distance(destinations[j][0], destinations[j][1], X0, Y0)\n                # Calculate the total damage\n                total_damage = dist1 + dist2 + dist3\n                # If the point is in the non-poisonous land, reduce the damage\n                if is_non_poisonous(destinations[i][0], destinations[i][1]) or is_non_poisonous(destinations[j][0], destinations[j][1]):\n                    total_damage -= 1\n                damages += total_damage\n\n    # Calculate the minimum damage\n    min_damage(X0, Y0, destinations)\n\n    # Print the number of times the character is damaged\n    print(damages)\n```\n\nThis script reads the input, processes the coordinates, and calculates the minimum number of damages based on the provided rules. It uses the `distance` function to calculate the distance between points and the `is_non_poisonous` function to check if a point is in the non-poisonous land. The `min_damage` function calculates the minimum damage by considering all possible routes between the destinations.",
