              "text": "To solve this problem, we need to identify which lunch menu should be endured to minimize the total calorie intake. Here's a step-by-step plan to achieve this:\n\n1. **Input the Calorie Values**: We will read three integers from the user input, representing the calories of the A, B, and C lunches.\n2. **Identify the Minimum Value**: Determine which of the three lunch options has the minimum calorie count. This will be the one that Kawabayashi will endure.\n3. **Output the Result**: Based on which lunch has the minimum calories, we will output the corresponding letter (A, B, or C).\n\nLet's write the Python script according to these steps:\n\n```python\n# Read the input values from the user\na, b, c = map(int, input().split())\n\n# Find the minimum value among the three inputs\nmin_value = min(a, b, c)\n\n# Determine which lunch corresponds to the minimum value and print the result\nif min_value == a:\n    print(\"A\")\nelif min_value == b:\n    print(\"B\")\nelse:\n    print(\"C\")\n```\n\n### Explanation:\n- `input().split()` reads a line of input and splits it into separate values.\n- `map(int, ...)` converts each of these values to integers.\n- `min(a, b, c)` finds the smallest number among the three integers.\n- The `if-elif-else` statements check which variable holds the minimum value and print the corresponding letter.\n\n### Example Test Cases:\n- For input `1000 900 850`, the minimum value is `850`, which corresponds to C lunch. So, the output is `C`.\n- For input `1000 800 1200`, the minimum value is `800`, which corresponds to B lunch. So, the output is `B`.\n- For input `1000 900 950`, the minimum value is `900`, which corresponds to B lunch. So, the output is `B`.\n\nThis script will work for any valid input according to the given constraints.",
