              "text": "To solve this problem, we need to calculate the number of times each staff member will step over the new cable. The cable is placed between two cells, and we need to determine the path each staff member takes and count the number of times they step over the cable.\n\nHere is the Python script to solve the problem:\n\n```python\n# Read input\nW, H, N = map(int, input().split())\nx1, y1, x2, y2 = map(int, input().split())\nstaff_positions = []\nstaff_patterns = []\n\n# Read staff positions and patterns\nfor _ in range(N):\n    x, y = map(int, input().split())\n    T, pattern = map(str, input().split())\n    T = int(T)\n    staff_positions.append((x, y))\n    staff_patterns.append((T, pattern))\n\n# Function to calculate the number of steps over the cable\ndef steps_over_cable(x, y, T, pattern, x1, y1, x2, y2):\n    steps = 0\n    for _ in range(T):\n        for move in pattern:\n            if move == 'U':\n                y -= 1\n            elif move == 'D':\n                y += 1\n            elif move == 'L':\n                x -= 1\n            elif move == 'R':\n                x += 1\n            # Check if the staff steps over the cable\n            if (x == x1 and y == y1) or (x == x2 and y == y2):\n                steps += 1\n    return steps\n\n# Calculate the total number of steps over the cable for all staff\ntotal_steps = 0\nfor x, y, T, pattern in zip(staff_positions, staff_patterns, staff_positions, staff_patterns):\n    total_steps += steps_over_cable(x, y, T, pattern[1], x1, y1, x2, y2)\n\n# Output the result\nprint(total_steps)\n```\n\nThis script reads the input, processes each staff member's position and pattern, and calculates the number of times they step over the cable. Finally, it outputs the total number of steps.",
