              "length": 591,
              "text": "To solve this problem, we need to determine the optimal placement of the new cable to minimize the number of times the staff step over the cable. We will follow these steps:\n\n1. Parse the input to get the dimensions of the office, the positions of the cable endpoints, and the staff's initial positions and movement patterns.\n2. Calculate the movement of each staff based on their initial position and movement pattern.\n3. Determine the number of times each staff will step over the cable.\n4. Sum the number of times all staff step over the cable and output the minimum number.\n\nLet's write the Python script to solve this problem:\n\n```python\n# Read input\nW, H, N = map(int, input().split())\nx1, y1, x2, y2 = map(int, input().split())\nstaff_positions = []\nstaff_patterns = []\n\nfor _ in range(N):\n    x, y = map(int, input().split())\n    T, pattern = input().split()\n    T = int(T)\n    staff_positions.append((x, y))\n    staff_patterns.append((T, pattern))\n\n# Function to move staff based on their pattern\ndef move_staff(x, y, pattern, T):\n    for _ in range(T):\n        for move in pattern:\n            if move == 'U':\n                y = max(0, y - 1)\n            elif move == 'D':\n                y = min(H - 1, y + 1)\n            elif move == 'L':\n                x = max(0, x - 1)\n            elif move == 'R':\n                x = min(W - 1, x + 1)\n    return x, y\n\n# Calculate the number of times each staff steps over the cable\ndef count_steps_over_cable(x1, y1, x2, y2, staff_positions, staff_patterns):\n    total_steps = 0\n    for x, y in staff_positions:\n        for T, pattern in staff_patterns:\n            x_end, y_end = move_staff(x, y, pattern, T)\n            # Check if the staff's final position intersects with the cable\n            if (x1 <= x_end <= x2 and y1 <= y_end <= y2) or (x1 <= x_end <= x2 and y1 <= y <= y2) or (x1 <= x <= x2 and y1 <= y_end <= y2):\n                total_steps += 1\n    return total_steps\n\n# Calculate the minimum number of times staff step over the cable\nresult = count_steps_over_cable(x1, y1, x2, y2, staff_positions, staff_patterns)\nprint(result)\n```\n\nThis script reads the input, processes the staff movements, and calculates the number of times each staff steps over the cable. It then prints the minimum number of times the staff step over the cable.",
