              "text": "To solve this problem, we need to simulate the movement of each staff member and count the number of times they step over the cable. Here's a step-by-step plan:\n\n1. Read the input values for the grid dimensions, number of staff, and the positions of the cable endpoints.\n2. Parse the initial positions and movement patterns of each staff member.\n3. Simulate the movement of each staff member based on their movement pattern.\n4. Count the number of times each staff member steps over the cable.\n5. Output the minimum number of times any staff member steps over the cable.\n\nLet's write the Python script to achieve this:\n\n```python\n# Read input\nW, H, N = map(int, input().split())\nx1, y1, x2, y2 = map(int, input().split())\ncable_positions = [(x1, y1), (x2, y2)]\n\n# Function to simulate staff movement and count steps over the cable\ndef simulate_staff(x, y, pattern, T, cable_positions):\n    steps_over_cable = 0\n    for _ in range(T):\n        for move in pattern:\n            if move == 'U':\n                y -= 1\n            elif move == 'D':\n                y += 1\n            elif move == 'L':\n                x -= 1\n            elif move == 'R':\n                x += 1\n            # Check if the new position is at the cable\n            if (x, y) in cable_positions:\n                steps_over_cable += 1\n    return steps_over_cable\n\n# Parse and simulate each staff member\nmin_steps = float('inf')\nfor _ in range(N):\n    x, y = map(int, input().split())\n    T, pattern = map(str, input().split())\n    T = int(T)\n    steps = simulate_staff(x, y, pattern, T, cable_positions)\n    min_steps = min(min_steps, steps)\n\n# Output the result\nprint(min_steps)\n```\n\nThis script reads the input, simulates the movement of each staff member, and counts the number of times they step over the cable. It then outputs the minimum number of times any staff member steps over the cable.",
