              "text": "Sure, let's break down the problem and write a Python script to solve it.\n\n### Problem Breakdown\n1. **Input**: The first line contains an integer \\( N \\), the number of squares. The second line contains \\( N \\) integers \\( H_1, H_2, \\ldots, H_N \\), where \\( H_i \\) is the height of the \\( i \\)-th square.\n2. **Process**: Starting from any square, move to the adjacent square on the right as long as the height of the next square is not greater than that of the current square.\n3. **Output**: The maximum number of times you can move.\n\n### Approach\n- Iterate through the list of heights.\n- Count the number of times you can move to the right while the height of the next square is not greater than the current square.\n\n### Python Script\n```python\n# Read input\nN = int(input())\nheights = list(map(int, input().split()))\n\n# Initialize the maximum number of moves\nmax_moves = 0\n\n# Iterate through the heights and count the number of moves\nfor i in range(N - 1):\n    moves = 0\n    while i < N - 1 and heights[i] >= heights[i + 1]:\n        moves += 1\n        i += 1\n    max_moves = max(max_moves, moves)\n\n# Output the result\nprint(max_moves)\n```\n\n### Explanation\n- **Input Reading**: We read the number of squares \\( N \\) and the list of heights.\n- **Loop through Heights**: We loop through the list of heights and count the number of moves for each starting position.\n- **Move Calculation**: For each starting position, we count the number of times we can move to the right while the height of the next square is not greater than the current square.\n- **Max Moves**: We keep track of the maximum number of moves found.\n\nThis script will correctly output the maximum number of times you can move based on the input provided.",
