              "text": "Sure, let's solve the problem step by step.\n\n### Problem Breakdown\n1. **Input:**\n   - The first line contains an integer \\( N \\), the number of squares.\n   - The second line contains \\( N \\) integers, \\( H_1, H_2, \\ldots, H_N \\), representing the heights of the squares.\n\n2. **Objective:**\n   - You start on any square and move to the right as long as the height of the next square is not greater than the current square.\n   - Find the maximum number of moves you can make.\n\n3. **Output:**\n   - Print the maximum number of times you can move.\n\n### Solution Approach\n- Iterate through the list of square heights.\n- For each square, count how many squares to the right have a height less than or equal to the current square's height.\n- Track the maximum count found during the iteration.\n\n### Python Script Implementation\nHere's how you can implement this:\n\n```python\n# Read input\nN = int(input())\nheights = list(map(int, input().split()))\n\n# Initialize the maximum number of moves to 0\nmax_moves = 0\n\n# Iterate through each square\nfor i in range(N):\n    moves = 0\n    current_height = heights[i]\n    # Move to the right as long as the next square is not greater\n    for j in range(i + 1, N):\n        if heights[j] <= current_height:\n            moves += 1\n        else:\n            break\n    # Update the maximum number of moves\n    max_moves = max(max_moves, moves)\n\n# Print the result\nprint(max_moves)\n```\n\n### Explanation\n1. **Input Reading:**\n   - `N` is the number of squares.\n   - `heights` is a list of integers representing the heights of the squares.\n\n2. **Initialization:**\n   - `max_moves` keeps track of the maximum number of moves found.\n\n3. **Iterate Through Each Square:**\n   - For each square `i`, initialize `moves` to 0.\n   - Use a nested loop to move to the right, counting valid moves as long as the next square's height is not greater than the current square's height.\n   - Update `max_moves` with the maximum value of `moves` found.\n\n4. **Output:**\n   - Print the maximum number of moves.\n\nThis code will correctly compute and output the maximum number of moves according to the given problem constraints and examples.",
