              "text": "To solve this problem, we need to find the subsequence of indices that maximizes the final output of the procedure, \\(x_{s_k}\\). We will use a brute-force approach to check all possible subsequences of length \\(k\\) and determine the one that gives the maximum value.\n\nHere is the Python script to solve the problem:\n\n```python\n# Read the number of formulae\nN = int(input())\n\n# Read the coefficients\na = list(map(int, input().split()))\n\n# Function to evaluate the subsequence\ndef evaluate_subsequence(s):\n    x = 1\n    for i in s:\n        x = a[i-1] * x\n    return x\n\n# Function to find the optimal subsequence\ndef find_optimal_subsequence(a, N):\n    max_value = float('-inf')\n    optimal_sequence = []\n    \n    # Generate all subsequences of length k\n    for k in range(N + 1):\n        for s in itertools.combinations(range(1, N + 1), k):\n            current_value = evaluate_subsequence(s)\n            if current_value > max_value:\n                max_value = current_value\n                optimal_sequence = s\n            elif current_value == max_value:\n                # Check for lexicographical order\n                if s < optimal_sequence:\n                    optimal_sequence = s\n    \n    return optimal_sequence\n\nimport itertools\n\n# Find the optimal subsequence\noptimal_sequence = find_optimal_subsequence(a, N)\n\n# Output the length of the sequence\nprint(len(optimal_sequence))\n# Output the indices of the sequence\nfor index in optimal_sequence:\n    print(index)\n```\n\nThis script first reads the number of formulae \\(N\\) and the coefficients \\(a_i\\). It then defines a function `evaluate_subsequence` to evaluate the output of a given subsequence. The function `find_optimal_subsequence` generates all possible subsequences of length \\(k\\) and finds the one that maximizes the final output, considering the lexicographical order. Finally, it outputs the length of the optimal subsequence and the indices of the subsequence.",
