              "text": "To solve this problem, we need to find the subsequence of indices that maximizes the final output of the procedure. We will use a brute-force approach to check all possible subsequences of length `k` and determine the one that gives the maximum final output. If there are multiple subsequences that give the same maximum output, we will choose the shortest one, and if there are still multiple, we will choose the lexicographically smallest one.\n\nHere is the Python script to solve the problem:\n\n```python\n# Read input\nN = int(input())\na = list(map(int, input().split()))\n\n# Function to evaluate the sequence\ndef evaluate_sequence(sequence):\n    x = 1\n    for i in sequence:\n        x = a[i-1] * x\n    return x\n\n# Function to find the optimal subsequence\ndef find_optimal_subsequence():\n    max_output = 0\n    optimal_sequence = []\n    \n    # Check all subsequences of length k\n    for k in range(1, N+1):\n        from itertools import combinations\n        for sequence in combinations(range(1, N+1), k):\n            output = evaluate_sequence(sequence)\n            if output > max_output or (output == max_output and len(sequence) < len(optimal_sequence)) or (output == max_output and len(sequence) == len(optimal_sequence) and sequence < optimal_sequence):\n                max_output = output\n                optimal_sequence = sequence\n    \n    return optimal_sequence\n\n# Find the optimal subsequence\noptimal_sequence = find_optimal_subsequence()\n\n# Output the result\nk = len(optimal_sequence)\nprint(k)\nfor i in optimal_sequence:\n    print(i)\n```\n\nThis script reads the input, defines a function to evaluate a sequence, and then finds the optimal subsequence that maximizes the final output. It outputs the length of the sequence and the indices of the elements in the sequence.",
