              "text": "Certainly! Let's break down the problem and create a Python script to solve it. The script will read three integers \\(a\\), \\(b\\), and \\(n\\) for each dataset, compute the sum \\(s\\) of the digits of the fraction \\(a / b\\) up to the \\(n\\)-th digit, and then print the result.\n\nHere's the step-by-step plan:\n1. Read the input values \\(a\\), \\(b\\), and \\(n\\).\n2. Compute the fraction \\(a / b\\) and extract the digits up to the \\(n\\)-th digit.\n3. Sum the digits.\n4. Print the sum \\(s\\).\n\nLet's write the Python script:\n\n```python\ndef compute_sum_of_digits(a, b, n):\n    # Compute the fraction a / b\n    fraction = a / b\n    \n    # Convert the fraction to a string to extract digits\n    fraction_str = str(fraction)\n    \n    # Remove the decimal point and get the first n digits after the decimal point\n    digits = fraction_str[fraction_str.index('.') + 1:][:n]\n    \n    # Convert each digit back to an integer and sum them\n    s = sum(int(digit) for digit in digits)\n    \n    return s\n\n# Read input\nwhile True:\n    try:\n        a, b, n = map(int, input().split())\n        s = compute_sum_of_digits(a, b, n)\n        print(s)\n    except EOFError:\n        break\n```\n\n### Explanation:\n1. **Function `compute_sum_of_digits`**:\n   - It takes \\(a\\), \\(b\\), and \\(n\\) as arguments.\n   - Computes the fraction \\(a / b\\).\n   - Converts the fraction to a string to easily extract digits.\n   - Extracts the first \\(n\\) digits after the decimal point.\n   - Sums these digits and returns the sum.\n\n2. **Main Loop**:\n   - Continuously reads input until the end of file (EOF).\n   - Splits the input into \\(a\\), \\(b\\), and \\(n\\).\n   - Calls the `compute_sum_of_digits` function and prints the result.\n\nThis script will handle multiple datasets as specified and print the sum of the digits of the fraction for each dataset.",
