              "text": "To solve this problem, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Parse the input to get the number of sequences \\(N\\) and the number of terms in each sequence \\(M\\).\n2. Read the sequences and store them.\n3. Sort the sequences lexicographically.\n4. Calculate the minimum number of spell casts needed to make the sequences strictly increasing lexicographically.\n\nHere's the Python script to achieve this:\n\n```python\n# Read the input\nN, M = map(int, input().split())\n\n# Initialize the sequences\nsequences = []\nfor _ in range(N):\n    sequences.append(list(map(int, input().split())))\n\n# Function to perform a spell cast on a sequence\ndef spell_cast(sequence):\n    return [sum(sequence[:i+1]) for i in range(M)]\n\n# Function to check if the sequences are sorted lexicographically\ndef is_sorted_lexicographically(sequences):\n    for i in range(len(sequences) - 1):\n        if sequences[i] >= sequences[i + 1]:\n            return False\n    return True\n\n# Function to find the minimum number of spell casts needed\ndef min_spells(sequences):\n    # Sort the sequences lexicographically\n    sorted_sequences = sorted(sequences)\n    \n    # If the sequences are already sorted, return 0\n    if sorted_sequences == sequences:\n        return 0\n    \n    # Initialize the number of casts\n    casts = 0\n    \n    # Iterate through the sequences\n    for i in range(N):\n        # If the current sequence is already in the correct position, continue\n        if sequences[i] == sorted_sequences[i]:\n            continue\n        \n        # Perform spell casts until the sequence is in the correct position\n        while sequences[i] != sorted_sequences[i]:\n            sequences[i] = spell_cast(sequences[i])\n            casts += 1\n    \n    # Check if the sequences are sorted after the casts\n    if is_sorted_lexicographically(sequences):\n        return casts\n    else:\n        return -1\n\n# Get the minimum number of casts\nresult = min_spells(sequences)\nprint(result)\n```\n\nThis script reads the input, processes the sequences, and calculates the minimum number of spell casts needed to make the sequences strictly increasing lexicographically. If it is not possible, it outputs `-1`.",
