              "length": 532,
              "text": "To solve this problem, we need to understand the process of casting the spell and how it affects the sequences. The spell turns a sequence \\( (a_1, a_2, \\ldots, a_M) \\) into \\( (s_1, s_2, \\ldots, s_M) \\) where \\( s_i = a_1 + a_2 + \\ldots + a_i \\). We need to find the minimum number of casts required to make the sequences \\( A_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_N \\) lexicographically increasing.\n\nHere is the step-by-step plan for the Python script:\n\n1. Read the input values \\( N \\) and \\( M \\).\n2. Read the \\( N \\) sequences.\n3. For each sequence, compute the sum sequence.\n4. Compare the sequences lexicographically and determine the number of casts needed to make them in the desired order.\n5. Return the minimum number of casts required or -1 if it is impossible.\n\nLet's write the Python script:\n\n```python\ndef min_casts(N, M, sequences):\n    # Initialize the number of casts\n    casts = 0\n    \n    # Iterate through the sequences\n    for i in range(1, N):\n        # Compare the current sequence with the previous one\n        for j in range(M):\n            if sequences[i][j] < sequences[i-1][j]:\n                # If the current sequence is smaller, no need to cast\n                break\n            elif sequences[i][j] > sequences[i-1][j]:\n                # If the current sequence is larger, we need to cast\n                casts += 1\n                # Update the current sequence\n                for k in range(j+1):\n                    sequences[i][k] = sum(sequences[i][:k+1])\n                break\n    \n    # Check if the sequences are in the correct order\n    for i in range(1, N):\n        for j in range(M):\n            if sequences[i][j] < sequences[i-1][j]:\n                return -1\n    \n    return casts\n\n# Read input\nN, M = map(int, input().split())\nsequences = []\nfor _ in range(N):\n    sequences.append(list(map(int, input().split())))\n\n# Calculate the minimum number of casts\nresult = min_casts(N, M, sequences)\nprint(result)\n```\n\nThis script reads the input, processes the sequences, and determines the minimum number of casts required to make the sequences lexicographically increasing. If it is impossible, it prints -1.",
