              "length": 478,
              "text": "To solve this problem, we need to understand the lexicographical order and the effect of casting the spell on each sequence. The spell turns a sequence \\( (a_1, a_2, \\ldots, a_M) \\) into \\( (s_1, s_2, \\ldots, s_M) \\) where \\( s_i = \\sum_{j=1}^{i} a_j \\).\n\nThe goal is to make the sequences \\( A_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_N \\) lexicographically ordered. We need to determine the minimum number of casts required to achieve this.\n\nHere is the step-by-step plan:\n1. Parse the input to get the sequences.\n2. Compare the sequences lexicographically.\n3. Determine the number of casts needed to transform the sequences into a lexicographically ordered sequence.\n\nLet's implement this in Python:\n\n```python\n# Read input\nN, M = map(int, input().split())\nsequences = []\nfor _ in range(N):\n    sequences.append(list(map(int, input().split())))\n\n# Function to perform the spell on a sequence\ndef cast_spell(sequence):\n    return [sum(sequence[:i+1]) for i in range(M)]\n\n# Function to count the number of casts needed\ndef count_casts(sequences):\n    casts_needed = 0\n    while True:\n        # Perform the spell on all sequences\n        transformed_sequences = [cast_spell(seq) for seq in sequences]\n        # Check if the sequences are in lexicographical order\n        is_sorted = True\n        for i in range(1, N):\n            if transformed_sequences[i] < transformed_sequences[i-1]:\n                is_sorted = False\n                break\n        if is_sorted:\n            return casts_needed\n        # If not sorted, increment the casts counter and continue\n        casts_needed += 1\n        # If the sequences cannot be sorted, return -1\n        if casts_needed > N * M:\n            return -1\n\n# Get the minimum number of casts needed\nresult = count_casts(sequences)\nprint(result)\n```\n\nThis script reads the input, processes the sequences, and calculates the minimum number of casts needed to make the sequences lexicographically ordered. If it is not possible to achieve the order, it outputs `-1`.",
