              "length": 439,
              "text": "To solve this problem, we need to understand the conditions under which the sequences can be ordered lexicographically by casting the spell. The spell transforms each sequence into a cumulative sum sequence, and we need to find the minimum number of such transformations required to ensure the sequences are in the desired order.\n\nHere is the step-by-step plan:\n1. Parse the input to get the number of sequences \\(N\\) and the length of each sequence \\(M\\).\n2. Read the sequences and store them.\n3. Compare the sequences lexicographically.\n4. Determine the minimum number of spell casts needed to make the sequences ordered.\n\nLet's write the Python script to implement this logic:\n\n```python\n# Read input\nN, M = map(int, input().split())\nsequences = []\nfor _ in range(N):\n    sequences.append(list(map(int, input().split())))\n\n# Function to perform the spell on a sequence\ndef perform_spell(sequence):\n    return [sum(sequence[:i+1]) for i in range(M)]\n\n# Function to check if sequence A is lexicographically smaller than sequence B\ndef is_lexicographically_smaller(A, B):\n    for i in range(M):\n        if A[i] < B[i]:\n            return True\n        elif A[i] > B[i]:\n            return False\n    return False\n\n# Function to count the minimum number of spell casts\ndef count_spell_casts(sequences):\n    spell_casts = 0\n    while True:\n        new_sequences = [perform_spell(seq) for seq in sequences]\n        if new_sequences == sorted(new_sequences):\n            return spell_casts\n        if not all(is_lexicographically_smaller(new_sequences[i], new_sequences[i+1]) for i in range(N-1)):\n            return -1\n        sequences = new_sequences\n        spell_casts += 1\n\n# Perform the spell casts and output the result\nresult = count_spell_casts(sequences)\nprint(result)\n```\n\nThis script reads the input, processes the sequences, and determines the minimum number of spell casts required to order the sequences lexicographically. If it is not possible, it outputs `-1`.",
