              "text": "To solve this problem, we need to calculate the area of a polygon given its vertices. The vertices are provided in a clockwise order, and we can use the Shoelace formula to compute the area.\n\nHere's the step-by-step plan:\n1. Read the number of vertices `n`.\n2. Read the coordinates of each vertex.\n3. Use the Shoelace formula to compute the area.\n4. Output the sequence number and the area.\n\nLet's implement this in Python:\n\n```python\n# Function to calculate the area using the Shoelace formula\ndef calculate_area(vertices):\n    n = len(vertices)\n    area = 0.0\n    for i in range(n):\n        x1, y1 = vertices[i]\n        x2, y2 = vertices[(i + 1) % n]\n        area += x1 * y2 - y1 * x2\n    area = abs(area) / 2.0\n    return area\n\n# Main program\nsequence_number = 1\nwhile True:\n    n = int(input())\n    if n == 0:\n        break\n    vertices = []\n    for _ in range(n):\n        x, y = map(int, input().split())\n        vertices.append((x, y))\n    area = calculate_area(vertices)\n    print(sequence_number, f\"{area:.1f}\")\n    sequence_number += 1\n```\n\nThis script will read the input, calculate the area of the polygon using the Shoelace formula, and output the sequence number and the area.",
