              "length": 447,
              "text": "To solve this problem, we need to calculate the area of a polygon given its vertices. The vertices are provided in a clockwise order, and the polygon is not necessarily convex. We can use the Shoelace formula (or Gauss's area formula) to compute the area of the polygon.\n\nThe Shoelace formula states that for a polygon with vertices \\((x_1, y_1), (x_2, y_2), \\ldots, (x_n, y_n)\\), the area \\(A\\) is given by:\n\\[\nA = \\frac{1}{2} \\left| \\sum_{i=1}^{n-1} (x_i y_{i+1} - y_i x_{i+1}) + (x_n y_1 - y_n x_1) \\right|\n\\]\n\nLet's write the Python script to implement this:\n\n```python\ndef calculate_area(vertices):\n    n = len(vertices)\n    area = 0.0\n    for i in range(n):\n        x1, y1 = vertices[i]\n        x2, y2 = vertices[(i + 1) % n]\n        area += x1 * y2 - y1 * x2\n    return abs(area) / 2.0\n\ndata_sets = []\nsequence_number = 1\n\nwhile True:\n    n = int(input())\n    if n == 0:\n        break\n    vertices = []\n    for _ in range(n):\n        x, y = map(int, input().split())\n        vertices.append((x, y))\n    area = calculate_area(vertices)\n    data_sets.append((sequence_number, area))\n    sequence_number += 1\n\nfor sequence, area in data_sets:\n    print(sequence, \"{:.1f}\".format(area))\n```\n\nThis script does the following:\n1. Reads the number of vertices \\(n\\) and the coordinates of each vertex.\n2. Uses the Shoelace formula to calculate the area of the polygon.\n3. Prints the sequence number and the area of the polygon with one digit after the decimal point.\n\nYou can run this script and input the data as specified to get the correct output.",
