              "length": 371,
              "text": "To solve this problem, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Read the input values for the sequence length \\( n \\) and the sequence \\( S \\).\n2. Perform the frequency operation on the sequence \\( S \\) to get the sequence \\( C \\).\n3. Repeat the frequency operation on the sequence \\( C \\) until the sequence becomes a fixed point \\( P \\).\n4. Count the number of frequency operations required to reach the fixed point.\n5. Output the number of operations and the fixed point sequence \\( P \\).\n\nLet's write the Python script to implement these steps:\n\n```python\ndef frequency_operation(sequence):\n    # Create a dictionary to count the frequency of each element\n    frequency_dict = {}\n    for element in sequence:\n        if element in frequency_dict:\n            frequency_dict[element] += 1\n        else:\n            frequency_dict[element] = 1\n    \n    # Create the new sequence based on the frequency counts\n    new_sequence = [frequency_dict[element] for element in sequence]\n    return new_sequence\n\ndef find_fixed_point(sequence):\n    original_sequence = sequence.copy()\n    count = 0\n    while True:\n        sequence = frequency_operation(sequence)\n        count += 1\n        if sequence == frequency_operation(sequence):\n            break\n    return count, sequence\n\n# Read input\nwhile True:\n    n = int(input())\n    if n == 0:\n        break\n    sequence = list(map(int, input().split()))\n    \n    # Find the fixed point and the number of operations\n    operations, fixed_point = find_fixed_point(sequence)\n    \n    # Output the results\n    print(operations)\n    print(' '.join(map(str, fixed_point)))\n```\n\nThis script reads the input, performs the frequency operations, and outputs the minimum number of operations and the fixed point sequence.",
