              "length": 271,
              "text": "To solve this problem, we need to follow the given criteria to compress the word sequence. Here's a step-by-step plan for the Python script:\n\n1. Read the number of words `N`.\n2. Read each word and store them in a list.\n3. Iterate through the list and check for redundant continuous subsequences based on the criteria.\n4. Remove the redundant subsequences and keep only the necessary words.\n5. Output the length of the compressed word sequence.\n\nLet's write the Python script to achieve this:\n\n```python\n# Read the number of words N\nN = int(input())\n\n# Read each word and store them in a list\nwords = []\nfor _ in range(N):\n    words.append(input().strip())\n\n# Initialize the compressed list with the first word\ncompressed_words = [words[0]]\n\n# Iterate through the words and compress\nfor i in range(1, N):\n    if compressed_words[-1][0] == words[i][0]:\n        continue\n    else:\n        compressed_words.append(words[i])\n\n# Output the length of the compressed word sequence\nprint(len(compressed_words))\n```\n\nThis script reads the number of words and the words themselves, then iterates through the list to remove redundant continuous subsequences based on the given criteria. Finally, it outputs the length of the compressed word sequence.",
