              "text": "To solve this problem, we need to follow the steps to compress the word sequence based on the given criteria. Here's the Python script that reads the input, processes the words, and outputs the minimum length of the compressed word sequence.\n\n```python\n# Read the number of words\nN = int(input())\n\n# Read the words\nwords = [input().strip() for _ in range(N)]\n\n# Initialize the compressed list with the first word\ncompressed = [words[0]]\n\n# Iterate through the words starting from the second one\nfor i in range(1, N):\n    current_word = words[i]\n    last_word = compressed[-1]\n    \n    # Check if the first letter of the current word matches the last letter of the last word in the compressed list\n    if current_word[0] == last_word[0]:\n        # Remove the last word in the compressed list\n        compressed.pop()\n    # Add the current word to the compressed list\n    compressed.append(current_word)\n\n# Output the length of the compressed list\nprint(len(compressed))\n```\n\nThis script reads the number of words and the words themselves, then processes them according to the given criteria to compress the sequence. It outputs the minimum length of the compressed word sequence.",
