              "text": "To solve this problem, we need to follow the given rules to compress the word sequence. Here's the step-by-step plan:\n\n1. Read the number of words `N`.\n2. Read each word and store them in a list.\n3. Iterate through the list and check if the first letter of the current word matches the first letter of the next word.\n4. If a match is found, remove the words between the matching words.\n5. Continue this process until no more matches are found.\n6. Count the number of remaining words and print the result.\n\nLet's implement this in Python:\n\n```python\n# Read the number of words\nN = int(input())\n\n# Read each word and store them in a list\nwords = []\nfor _ in range(N):\n    word = input().strip()\n    words.append(word)\n\n# Function to compress the word sequence\ndef compress_sequence(words):\n    i = 0\n    while i < len(words) - 1:\n        if words[i][0] == words[i + 1][0]:\n            # Remove the words between the matching words\n            j = i + 1\n            while j < len(words) and words[j][0] == words[i][0]:\n                j += 1\n            words = words[:i] + words[j:]\n        else:\n            i += 1\n    return words\n\n# Compress the word sequence\ncompressed_words = compress_sequence(words)\n\n# Output the number of remaining words\nprint(len(compressed_words))\n```\n\nThis script reads the number of words and each word, then compresses the sequence according to the given rules, and finally prints the number of remaining words.",
