              "text": "To solve this problem, we need to compress the word sequence by removing redundant continuous subsequences based on the criteria provided. Here's a step-by-step approach to achieve this:\n\n1. Read the number of words \\( N \\) and the list of words.\n2. Iterate through the list of words and check for redundant continuous subsequences.\n3. Remove the redundant continuous subsequences.\n4. Count the number of words in the compressed sequence.\n5. Output the count.\n\nLet's write the Python script to implement this logic:\n\n```python\n# Read the number of words\nN = int(input())\n\n# Read the list of words\nwords = []\nfor _ in range(N):\n    word = input()\n    words.append(word)\n\n# Function to compress the word sequence\ndef compress_sequence(words):\n    compressed_words = []\n    i = 0\n    while i < len(words):\n        current_word = words[i]\n        j = i + 1\n        while j < len(words) and words[j][0] == current_word[0]:\n            j += 1\n        compressed_words.append(current_word)\n        i = j\n    return compressed_words\n\n# Compress the word sequence\ncompressed_words = compress_sequence(words)\n\n# Output the number of words in the compressed sequence\nprint(len(compressed_words))\n```\n\nThis script reads the number of words and the list of words, then compresses the sequence by removing redundant continuous subsequences, and finally outputs the number of words in the compressed sequence.",
