              "contract_reward": 0.1,
              "length": 267,
              "text": "To solve this problem, we need to iterate through all pairs of attendees and check if the condition is satisfied. The condition is that the absolute difference of their attendee numbers is equal to the sum of their heights.\n\nHere's the step-by-step plan:\n1. Read the number of attendees `N`.\n2. Read the heights of the attendees.\n3. Iterate through all pairs of attendees.\n4. For each pair, check if the absolute difference of their attendee numbers is equal to the sum of their heights.\n5. Count the number of pairs that satisfy the condition.\n6. Print the count.\n\nLet's write the Python script to implement this plan:\n\n```python\n# Read the number of attendees\nN = int(input())\n\n# Read the heights of the attendees\nheights = list(map(int, input().split()))\n\n# Initialize the count of valid pairs\ncount = 0\n\n# Iterate through all pairs of attendees\nfor i in range(N):\n    for j in range(i + 1, N):\n        if abs(i - j) == heights[i] + heights[j]:\n            count += 1\n\n# Print the count of valid pairs\nprint(count)\n```\n\nThis script reads the number of attendees and their heights, then iterates through all possible pairs to count the number of pairs that satisfy the condition.",
