              "text": "To solve this problem, we need to count the number of pairs of attendees that satisfy the given condition. The condition is that the absolute difference of their attendee numbers is equal to the sum of their heights.\n\nHere is the step-by-step plan for the Python script:\n\n1. Read the number of attendees \\( N \\) and the heights of each attendee \\( A_i \\).\n2. Iterate through all possible pairs of attendees.\n3. For each pair, check if the absolute difference of their attendee numbers is equal to the sum of their heights.\n4. Count the number of pairs that satisfy the condition.\n5. Print the count.\n\nLet's write the Python script:\n\n```python\n# Read the number of attendees\nN = int(input())\n\n# Read the heights of each attendee\nheights = list(map(int, input().split()))\n\n# Initialize the count of valid pairs\ncount = 0\n\n# Iterate through all possible pairs of attendees\nfor i in range(N):\n    for j in range(i + 1, N):\n        # Check if the absolute difference of their attendee numbers is equal to the sum of their heights\n        if abs(i - j) == heights[i] + heights[j]:\n            count += 1\n\n# Print the count of valid pairs\nprint(count)\n```\n\nThis script will read the input, process the pairs, and output the number of pairs that satisfy the condition.",
