              "text": "To solve this problem, we need to iterate through all possible pairs of attendees and check if the condition is satisfied. The condition is that the absolute difference of their attendee numbers is equal to the sum of their heights. We can use a dictionary to keep track of the heights and then check the condition for each pair.\n\nHere is the Python script to solve the problem:\n\n```python\n# Read the number of attendees\nN = int(input())\n\n# Read the heights of the attendees\nA = list(map(int, input().split()))\n\n# Initialize a counter for the number of valid pairs\ncount = 0\n\n# Iterate through each pair of attendees\nfor i in range(N):\n    for j in range(i + 1, N):\n        # Check if the absolute difference of their attendee numbers is equal to the sum of their heights\n        if abs(i - j) == A[i] + A[j]:\n            count += 1\n\n# Print the number of pairs satisfying the condition\nprint(count)\n```\n\nThis script reads the number of attendees and their heights, then iterates through all possible pairs to check the condition. It counts and prints the number of pairs that satisfy the condition.",
