              "contract_reward": 0.1,
              "length": 645,
              "text": "To solve this problem, we need to simulate the movement of the hexerpent in the hexagonal grid. The hexerpent can move its sections at its either end to up to two dimples, and can move intermediate sections to only one dimple, if any. The goal is to find the minimum number of steps required for the hexerpent's head to reach the scientist's position.\n\nHere's the Python script to solve this problem:\n\n```python\nimport sys\nfrom collections import deque\n\ndef distance(p1, p2):\n    return abs(p1[0] - p2[0]) + abs(p1[1] - p2[1])\n\ndef is_adjacent(p1, p2):\n    return distance(p1, p2) == 1\n\ndef find_path(n, sections, rocks, goal):\n    queue = deque([(sections[0], 0)])\n    visited = set([sections[0]])\n    \n    while queue:\n        current, steps = queue.popleft()\n        \n        if current == goal:\n            return steps\n        \n        # Try moving the head to the next position\n        for i in range(1, min(3, n)):\n            next_pos = (current[0] + i, current[1])\n            if next_pos not in visited and not is_adjacent(next_pos, sections[i]) and not next_pos in rocks:\n                visited.add(next_pos)\n                queue.append((next_pos, steps + 1))\n        \n        # Try moving the tail to the previous position\n        for i in range(n-2, -1, -1):\n            next_pos = (current[0] - i, current[1])\n            if next_pos not in visited and not is_adjacent(next_pos, sections[i]) and not next_pos in rocks:\n                visited.add(next_pos)\n                queue.append((next_pos, steps + 1))\n        \n        # Try moving intermediate sections\n        for i in range(1, n-1):\n            next_pos = (current[0] + 1, current[1])\n            if next_pos not in visited and not is_adjacent(next_pos, sections[i]) and not next_pos in rocks:\n                visited.add(next_pos)\n                queue.append((next_pos, steps + 1))\n    \n    return -1\n\nwhile True:\n    n = int(input())\n    if n == 0:\n        break\n    \n    sections = []\n    for _ in range(n):\n        x, y = map(int, input().split())\n        sections.append((x, y))\n    \n    k = int(input())\n    rocks = []\n    for _ in range(k):\n        u, v = map(int, input().split())\n        rocks.append((u, v))\n    \n    X, Y = map(int, input().split())\n    goal = (X, Y)\n    \n    print(find_path(n, sections, rocks, goal))\n```\n\nThis script reads the input, processes the hexerpent's sections and rocks, and then uses a breadth-first search (BFS) to find the minimum number of steps required for the hexerpent's head to reach the goal position.",
