              "text": "To solve this problem, we need to simulate the sales activities as described. We will use a list to keep track of the incubated individuals and handle the four types of queries as specified. Let's break down the solution step-by-step:\n\n1. **Reading Input**: We need to read the input and process each query.\n2. **Handling Queries**: We will handle each query type (0, 1, 2, 3) accordingly.\n3. **Output**: We will output the results as required.\n\nHere is the Python script to achieve this:\n\n```python\n# Read input\nq, lim = map(int, input().split())\n\n# Initialize the list to store the incubated individuals\nindividuals = []\n\n# Process each query\nfor _ in range(q):\n    query, x = map(int, input().split())\n    if query == 0:\n        # Incubate an individual and assign a number\n        individuals.append(x)\n    elif query == 1:\n        # Lead the individual indicated by the nth number of the array to the theory of the ring\n        if x <= len(individuals):\n            individuals.pop(x - 1)\n    elif query == 2:\n        # Output the number of the xth individual contained in the array at that time\n        if x <= len(individuals):\n            print(individuals[x - 1])\n        else:\n            print(\"end\")\n    elif query == 3:\n        # Lead the individual with the number xi to the theory of the ring\n        if x in individuals:\n            individuals.remove(x)\n\n# Print \"end\" at the end of each case\nprint(\"end\")\n```\n\n### Explanation:\n1. **Reading Input**: We first read the number of queries `q` and the limit `lim`.\n2. **Handling Queries**:\n   - **Query 0**: Add the individual number to the list.\n   - **Query 1**: Remove the individual at the specified position.\n   - **Query 2**: Print the individual at the specified position.\n   - **Query 3**: Remove the individual with the specified number.\n3. **Output**: Print \"end\" at the end of each case.\n\nThis script will correctly handle the input and output as specified in the problem statement.",
