              "text": "To solve this problem, we need to simulate the sales activities based on the log file. We will use a list to keep track of the incubated individuals and handle the different queries accordingly. Here is the Python script to achieve this:\n\n```python\ndef main():\n    while True:\n        q, lim = map(int, input().split())\n        if q == 0 and lim == 0:\n            break\n        \n        # Initialize the list to store the incubated individuals\n        incubated_individuals = []\n        \n        for _ in range(q):\n            query, x = map(int, input().split())\n            if query == 0:\n                # Incubate an individual and assign a number\n                incubated_individuals.append(x)\n            elif query == 1:\n                # Lead the individual indicated by the nth number of the array to the theory of the ring\n                if len(incubated_individuals) >= lim:\n                    incubated_individuals.pop(0)\n                incubated_individuals.pop(x - 1)\n            elif query == 2:\n                # Output the number of the xth individual contained in the array at that time\n                if 1 <= x <= len(incubated_individuals):\n                    print(incubated_individuals[x - 1])\n                else:\n                    print(\"Invalid index\")\n            elif query == 3:\n                # Lead the individual with the number x to the theory of the ring\n                if x in incubated_individuals:\n                    incubated_individuals.remove(x)\n                else:\n                    print(\"Individual not found\")\n        \n        print(\"end\")\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```\n\nThis script reads the input, processes the queries, and outputs the results based on the provided log file. It handles the different types of queries as specified and ensures that the list of incubated individuals is managed correctly according to the rules.",
