              "length": 401,
              "text": "To solve this problem, we need to implement a program that can process the log file entries and perform the required operations on an array of individual numbers. The operations include incubating individuals, removing individuals from the ring theory, and querying the individual numbers at specific positions.\n\nHere is the Python script to achieve this:\n\n```python\ndef process_log_file(q, lim, queries):\n    if q == 0:\n        return\n    \n    # Initialize the array to store individual numbers\n    individuals = []\n    \n    for query, x in queries:\n        if query == 0:\n            # Incubate an individual and assign a number\n            individuals.append(x)\n            if len(individuals) > lim:\n                # Remove the first individual if the limit is exceeded\n                individuals.pop(0)\n        elif query == 1:\n            # Remove the individual at position x\n            if 1 <= x <= len(individuals):\n                individuals.pop(x-1)\n        elif query == 2:\n            # Query the individual number at position x\n            if 1 <= x <= len(individuals):\n                print(individuals[x-1])\n            else:\n                print(\"end\")\n        elif query == 3:\n            # Remove the individual with number x\n            for i, ind in enumerate(individuals):\n                if ind == x:\n                    individuals.pop(i)\n                    break\n        else:\n            print(\"Invalid query\")\n    \n    print(\"end\")\n\n# Read input\nwhile True:\n    q, lim = map(int, input().split())\n    if q == 0 and lim == 0:\n        break\n    queries = [list(map(int, input().split())) for _ in range(q)]\n    process_log_file(q, lim, queries)\n```\n\nThis script reads the input, processes the log file entries, and performs the required operations on the array of individual numbers. It handles the four types of queries as specified and prints the results as required.",
