              "text": "To solve this problem, we need to simulate the movement of the ninja on the polygon. The key steps are:\n\n1. Parse the input to get the number of vertices, start and goal points, and the vertices of the polygon.\n2. Implement the movement logic, including handling diagonal and perpendicular movements, as well as movements along the walls.\n3. Use a breadth-first search (BFS) to find the shortest path from the start point to the goal point.\n\nHere is the Python script to solve the problem:\n\n```python\nimport sys\nfrom collections import deque\n\n# Function to check if a point is inside the polygon\ndef is_inside_polygon(x, y, vertices):\n    n = len(vertices)\n    inside = False\n    p1x, p1y = vertices[0]\n    for i in range(n + 1):\n        p2x, p2y = vertices[i % n]\n        if y > min(p1y, p2y):\n            if y <= max(p1y, p2y):\n                if x <= max(p1x, p2x):\n                    if p1y != p2y:\n                        xinters = (y - p1y) * (p2x - p1x) / (p2y - p1y) + p1x\n                    if p1x == p2x or x <= xinters:\n                        inside = not inside\n        p1x, p1y = p2x, p2y\n    return inside\n\n# Function to move the ninja\ndef move_ninja(x, y, direction):\n    dx, dy = 0, 0\n    if direction == 'U':\n        dy = -1\n    elif direction == 'D':\n        dy = 1\n    elif direction == 'L':\n        dx = -1\n    elif direction == 'R':\n        dx = 1\n    elif direction == 'UL':\n        dx, dy = -1, -1\n    elif direction == 'UR':\n        dx, dy = 1, -1\n    elif direction == 'DL':\n        dx, dy = -1, 1\n    elif direction == 'DR':\n        dx, dy = 1, 1\n    new_x, new_y = x + dx, y + dy\n    return new_x, new_y\n\n# Function to find the minimum number of commands\ndef find_min_commands(sx, sy, gx, gy, vertices):\n    queue = deque([(sx, sy, '')])\n    visited = set([(sx, sy)])\n    while queue:\n        x, y, command = queue.popleft()\n        if (x, y) == (gx, gy):\n            return len(command)\n        for direction in ['U', 'D', 'L', 'R', 'UL', 'UR', 'DL', 'DR']:\n            new_x, new_y = move_ninja(x, y, direction)\n            if is_inside_polygon(new_x, new_y, vertices) and (new_x, new_y) not in visited:\n                visited.add((new_x, new_y))\n                queue.append((new_x, new_y, command + direction))\n    return -1\n\n# Read input\nwhile True:\n    N = int(input())\n    if N == 0:\n        break\n    sx, sy, gx, gy = map(int, input().split())\n    vertices = []\n    for _ in range(N):\n        x, y = map(int, input().split())\n        vertices.append((x, y))\n    # Find and print the minimum number of commands\n    print(find_min_commands(sx, sy, gx, gy, vertices))\n```\n\nThis script reads the input, processes each dataset, and outputs the minimum number of commands required to move from the start point to the goal point.",
