              "text": "Certainly! Let's break down the problem and write the Python script to solve it.\n\n### Problem Breakdown:\n- We need to calculate the number of set bits (bits that are 1) in the binary representation of each number in the range [A, B].\n- We then sum these values for all numbers in the range.\n- We need to do this for multiple test cases.\n\n### Steps to Solve:\n1. Read the number of test cases.\n2. For each test case, read the values of A and B.\n3. Iterate through the range [A, B] and calculate the number of set bits for each number.\n4. Sum the set bits for all numbers in the range.\n5. Output the result for each test case.\n\n### Python Script:\n```python\ndef count_set_bits(n):\n    count = 0\n    while n:\n        count += n & 1\n        n >>= 1\n    return count\n\ndef solve_test_case(A, B):\n    total_set_bits = 0\n    for x in range(A, B + 1):\n        total_set_bits += count_set_bits(x)\n    return total_set_bits\n\n# Read the number of test cases\nT = int(input())\n\n# Process each test case\nfor _ in range(T):\n    A, B = map(int, input().split())\n    result = solve_test_case(A, B)\n    print(result)\n```\n\n### Explanation:\n- `count_set_bits(n)`: This function counts the number of set bits in the binary representation of `n`.\n- `solve_test_case(A, B)`: This function calculates the sum of set bits for all numbers in the range [A, B].\n- The script reads the number of test cases, processes each test case, and outputs the result.\n\n### Sample Input and Output:\n- **Input:**\n  ```\n  1\n  1 3\n  ```\n- **Output:**\n  ```\n  4\n  ```\n\nThis script will correctly handle the given constraints and sample input.",
