              "length": 666,
              "text": "To solve this problem, we need to determine the time interval within which all the watches have at least one candidate time. Here's a step-by-step plan to achieve this:\n\n1. **Input Parsing**: Read the number of watches and their positions.\n2. **Generate Candidates**: For each watch, generate all possible times by rotating the hands and permuting the hands.\n3. **Check Validity**: For each candidate time, check if it is a valid time on a watch.\n4. **Find Intersection**: Find the intersection of all candidate times for all watches.\n5. **Output Result**: Output the shortest time interval.\n\nLet's write the Python script to implement this plan.\n\n```python\ndef generate_candidates(s, t, u):\n    # Generate all possible times by rotating the hands and permuting the hands\n    candidates = set()\n    hands = [s, t, u]\n    for i in range(60):\n        for j in range(60):\n            for k in range(60):\n                # Rotate the hands\n                hand1 = (s + i) % 60\n                hand2 = (t + j) % 60\n                hand3 = (u + k) % 60\n                # Permute the hands\n                for perm in [(0, 1, 2), (0, 2, 1), (1, 0, 2), (1, 2, 0), (2, 0, 1), (2, 1, 0)]:\n                    hour = hand1 // 20\n                    minute = (hand2 // 10) % 6\n                    second = hand3 % 10\n                    if hour < 12 and minute < 60 and second < 60:\n                        candidates.add((hour, minute, second))\n    return candidates\n\ndef find_shortest_interval(candidates):\n    min_time = (12, 60, 60)\n    max_time = (0, 0, 0)\n    for cand in candidates:\n        if cand < min_time:\n            min_time = cand\n        if cand > max_time:\n            max_time = cand\n    return min_time, max_time\n\nwhile True:\n    n = int(input())\n    if n == 0:\n        break\n    candidates = []\n    for _ in range(n):\n        s, t, u = map(int, input().split())\n        candidates.append(generate_candidates(s, t, u))\n    \n    # Find the intersection of all candidate times\n    intersection = set(candidates[0])\n    for cand_set in candidates[1:]:\n        intersection &= cand_set\n    \n    # Find the shortest time interval\n    min_time, max_time = find_shortest_interval(intersection)\n    print(f\"{min_time[0]:02}:{min_time[1]:02}:{min_time[2]:02} {max_time[0]:02}:{max_time[1]:02}:{max_time[2]:02}\")\n```\n\nThis script reads the input, generates all possible times for each watch, finds the intersection of all candidate times, and outputs the shortest time interval.",
