              "text": "To solve this problem, we need to consider the positions of the three hands on the watches and calculate the possible times they could represent. We will then find the shortest time interval that includes all the possible times from the given watches.\n\nHere is the Python script to solve the problem:\n\n```python\ndef calculate_time(s, t, u):\n    # Calculate the hour, minute, and second based on the ticks\n    hour = s // 360\n    minute = t // 6\n    second = u\n    return (hour, minute, second)\n\ndef find_possible_times(s, t, u):\n    possible_times = []\n    for i in range(12):\n        for j in range(60):\n            for k in range(60):\n                if (i * 360 + j * 6 + k) % 360 == (s * 360 + t * 6 + u) % 360:\n                    possible_times.append((i, j, k))\n    return possible_times\n\ndef find_shortest_interval(watches):\n    all_possible_times = []\n    for watch in watches:\n        s, t, u = watch\n        possible_times = find_possible_times(s, t, u)\n        all_possible_times.append(possible_times)\n    \n    # Find the intersection of all possible times\n    intersection_times = all_possible_times[0]\n    for possible_times in all_possible_times[1:]:\n        intersection_times = [time for time in intersection_times if time in possible_times]\n    \n    # Convert the times to the format hh:mm:ss\n    times = []\n    for time in intersection_times:\n        hour, minute, second = time\n        times.append(f\"{hour:02}:{minute:02}:{second:02}\")\n    \n    # Find the shortest interval\n    shortest_interval = None\n    for i in range(len(times)):\n        for j in range(i + 1, len(times)):\n            start_time = times[i]\n            end_time = times[j]\n            if shortest_interval is None or (int(end_time.replace(\":\", \"\")) - int(start_time.replace(\":\", \"\"))) < (int(shortest_interval[1].replace(\":\", \"\")) - int(shortest_interval[0].replace(\":\", \"\"))):\n                shortest_interval = [start_time, end_time]\n    \n    return shortest_interval\n\nwhile True:\n    n = int(input())\n    if n == 0:\n        break\n    \n    watches = []\n    for _ in range(n):\n        s, t, u = map(int, input().split())\n        watches.append((s, t, u))\n    \n    shortest_interval = find_shortest_interval(watches)\n    print(f\"{shortest_interval[0]} {shortest_interval[1]}\")\n```\n\nThis script reads the number of watches and their positions, calculates the possible times for each watch, finds the intersection of all possible times, and then determines the shortest time interval that includes all the possible times.",
