              "text": "To solve this problem, we need to determine the possible times for each watch and then find the shortest interval that includes all possible times from all watches. Here's the step-by-step plan:\n\n1. **Parse the Input**: Read the number of watches and their hand positions.\n2. **Generate Possible Times**: For each watch, generate all possible times considering rotations and permutations of the hands.\n3. **Find Overlapping Intervals**: For each pair of watches, determine the overlapping time intervals.\n4. **Determine Shortest Interval**: Find the shortest interval that covers all watches.\n\nLet's write the Python script to solve this problem.\n\n```python\ndef generate_possible_times(s, t, u):\n    times = set()\n    # Generate all permutations of the hands\n    hands_permutations = [(s, t, u), (s, u, t), (t, s, u), (t, u, s), (u, s, t), (u, t, s)]\n    for h, m, s in hands_permutations:\n        # Generate all rotations of the hands\n        for i in range(12):\n            hour = (h + i * 60) % 720 // 60\n            minute = (m + i * 60) % 60\n            second = (s + i * 60) % 60\n            times.add((hour, minute, second))\n    return times\n\ndef find_shortest_interval(watches):\n    n = len(watches)\n    # Generate all possible times for each watch\n    all_times = [generate_possible_times(*watch) for watch in watches]\n    \n    # Helper function to find the intersection of two sets of times\n    def intersect_times(t1, t2):\n        return t1.intersection(t2)\n    \n    # Find the intersection of all sets of times\n    if n == 2:\n        intersection = intersect_times(all_times[0], all_times[1])\n    else:\n        intersection = all_times[0]\n        for i in range(1, n):\n            intersection = intersect_times(intersection, all_times[i])\n    \n    # Convert the set of times to a sorted list\n    intersection_list = sorted(intersection)\n    if not intersection_list:\n        return \"No common time\"\n    \n    # Determine the shortest interval\n    min_start = intersection_list[0]\n    max_end = min_start\n    for i in range(1, len(intersection_list)):\n        if intersection_list[i][0] != (min_start[0] + 1) % 12:\n            current_end = intersection_list[i - 1]\n            if current_end[0] == (min_start[0] + 1) % 12:\n                if current_end[1] != (min_start[1] + 1) % 60:\n                    current_end = (current_end[0], (min_start[1] + 1) % 60, 0)\n                    if current_end < intersection_list[i]:\n                        intersection_list[i - 1] = current_end\n                else:\n                    current_end = (current_end[0], (min_start[1] + 1) % 60, (min_start[2] + 1) % 60)\n                    if current_end < intersection_list[i]:\n                        intersection_list[i - 1] = current_end\n            else:\n                if intersection_list[i][1] != (min_start[1] + 1) % 60:\n                    current_end = (intersection_list[i - 1][0], (min_start[1] + 1) % 60, 0)\n                    if current_end < intersection_list[i]:\n                        intersection_list[i - 1] = current_end\n                else:\n                    current_end = (intersection_list[i - 1][0], (min_start[1] + 1) % 60, (min_start[2] + 1) % 60)\n                    if current_end < intersection_list[i]:\n                        intersection_list[i - 1] = current_end\n            if current_end > max_end:\n                max_end = current_end\n            min_start = intersection_list[i]\n    \n    # Convert the times to the required format\n    start_time = f\"{min_start[0]:02}:{min_start[1]:02}:{min_start[2]:02}\"\n    end_time = f\"{max_end[0]:02}:{max_end[1]:02}:{max_end[2]:02}\"\n    return start_time + \" \" + end_time\n\n# Main loop to process each dataset\nwhile True:\n    n = int(input())\n    if n == 0:\n        break\n    watches = []\n    for _ in range(n):\n        s, t, u = map(int, input().split())\n        watches.append((s, t, u))\n    \n    result = find_shortest_interval(watches)\n    print(result)\n```\n\n### Explanation:\n1. **Generating Possible Times**: For each watch, we generate all possible times considering rotations and permutations of the hands.\n2. **Finding Overlapping Intervals**: We find the intersection of all possible times for all watches.\n3. **Determining the Shortest Interval**: We determine the shortest interval that includes all possible times from all watches and convert the times to the required format.\n\nThis script will read the input, process each dataset, and output the shortest time interval that includes all possible times for the given watches.",
