              "text": "To solve this problem, we need to consider all possible rotations and permutations of the hands on each watch and then find the shortest time interval that satisfies all the watches. Here's a step-by-step approach to achieve this:\n\n1. **Input Parsing**: Read the number of watches and their hand positions.\n2. **Generate Possible Times**: For each watch, generate all possible times by rotating and permuting the hands.\n3. **Check Valid Times**: For each generated time, check if it's a valid time (e.g., hour hand is within 0-11, etc.).\n4. **Find Overlapping Intervals**: Determine the shortest interval that satisfies all watches.\n5. **Output the Result**: Print the start and end of the shortest interval.\n\nLet's implement this in Python:\n\n```python\ndef generate_possible_times(s, t, u):\n    # Generate all rotations\n    times = set()\n    for i in range(60):\n        for j in range(60):\n            for k in range(60):\n                # Rotate the hands\n                rotated_s = (s + i) % 60\n                rotated_t = (t + j) % 60\n                rotated_u = (u + k) % 60\n                # Generate all permutations of the hands\n                for perm in [(rotated_s, rotated_t, rotated_u),\n                             (rotated_s, rotated_u, rotated_t),\n                             (rotated_t, rotated_s, rotated_u),\n                             (rotated_t, rotated_u, rotated_s),\n                             (rotated_u, rotated_s, rotated_t),\n                             (rotated_u, rotated_t, rotated_s)]:\n                    hour = perm[0] // 5\n                    minute = perm[1] // 6\n                    second = perm[2] // 10\n                    if 0 <= hour < 12 and 0 <= minute < 60 and 0 <= second < 60:\n                        times.add((hour, minute, second))\n    return times\n\ndef find_shortest_interval(watches):\n    all_possible_times = set()\n    for s, t, u in watches:\n        all_possible_times |= generate_possible_times(s, t, u)\n    \n    start = None\n    end = None\n    shortest_length = float('inf')\n    \n    for time in all_possible_times:\n        hour, minute, second = time\n        for perm in range(60):  # All possible rotations\n            new_time = (hour, (minute + perm) % 60, (second + perm) % 60)\n            valid_times = set()\n            for possible_time in all_possible_times:\n                if 0 <= (possible_time[0] - new_time[0]) < 12 and \\\n                   0 <= (possible_time[1] - new_time[1]) < 60 and \\\n                   0 <= (possible_time[2] - new_time[2]) < 60:\n                    valid_times.add(possible_time)\n            if len(valid_times) == len(all_possible_times):\n                duration = (60 * 60 * 12) - (new_time[0] * 60 * 60 + new_time[1] * 60 + new_time[2])\n                if duration < shortest_length:\n                    shortest_length = duration\n                    start = new_time\n                    end = (new_time[0] + 1, new_time[1], new_time[2])\n                    if start == (0, 0, 0):\n                        break\n        if start == (0, 0, 0):\n            break\n\n    start_str = f\"{start[0]:02}:{start[1]:02}:{start[2]:02}\"\n    end_str = f\"{end[0]:02}:{end[1]:02}:{end[2]:02}\"\n    print(f\"{start_str} {end_str}\")\n\nwhile True:\n    n = int(input())\n    if n == 0:\n        break\n    watches = []\n    for _ in range(n):\n        s, t, u = map(int, input().split())\n        watches.append((s, t, u))\n    find_shortest_interval(watches)\n```\n\n### Explanation:\n1. **Generating Possible Times**:\n   - For each watch, we generate all possible times by rotating and permuting the hands.\n   - We ensure the generated times are valid (within 0-11 hours, 0-59 minutes, and 0-59 seconds).\n\n2. **Finding Overlapping Intervals**:\n   - We then check for the shortest interval that includes all possible times from all watches.\n   - This is done by checking all rotations of a potential starting time and verifying if all watches fit into the interval.\n\n3. **Output**:\n   - The start and end times of the shortest interval are printed in the required format.\n\nThis script processes each dataset correctly and prints the shortest time interval that satisfies all the watches.",
