              "text": "To solve this problem, we need to follow the steps below:\n\n1. Parse the input to extract the glyph dictionary and the monoliths.\n2. Identify the glyphs and their corresponding characters.\n3. Identify the monoliths and their bitmaps.\n4. Determine the direction of the sequence (left to right or right to left).\n5. Transliterate the sequence based on the direction and the glyph dictionary.\n6. Output the transliterated sequence for each monolith.\n\nHere is the Python script to achieve this:\n\n```python\ndef parse_glyph(glyph):\n    c, h, w = map(int, glyph.split())\n    return c, h, w, [input() for _ in range(h)]\n\ndef parse_monolith(string):\n    h, w = map(int, string.split())\n    return [input() for _ in range(h)]\n\ndef find_glyph(glyph_dict, bitmap):\n    for c, h, w, bitmap_dict in glyph_dict:\n        if h == len(bitmap) and w == len(bitmap[0]):\n            if all(bitmap[i][j] == bitmap_dict[i][j] for i in range(h) for j in range(w)):\n                return c\n    return None\n\ndef find_box(glyph_dict, bitmap):\n    for c, h, w, bitmap_dict in glyph_dict:\n        if h == len(bitmap) and w == len(bitmap[0]):\n            if all(bitmap[i][j] == bitmap_dict[i][j] for i in range(h) for j in range(w)):\n                return c\n    return None\n\ndef flip_bitmap(bitmap):\n    return [\"\".join(row[::-1]) for row in bitmap]\n\ndef is_flipped(glyph_dict, bitmap):\n    flipped_bitmap = flip_bitmap(bitmap)\n    for c, h, w, bitmap_dict in glyph_dict:\n        if h == len(bitmap) and w == len(bitmap[0]):\n            if all(bitmap[i][j] == bitmap_dict[i][j] for i in range(h) for j in range(w)):\n                return True\n    return False\n\ndef transliterate_sequence(glyph_dict, sequence):\n    sequence_list = []\n    for row in sequence:\n        if any(row[i] == '*' for i in range(len(row))):\n            sequence_list.append(find_box(glyph_dict, row))\n        else:\n            sequence_list.append(find_glyph(glyph_dict, row))\n    if is_flipped(glyph_dict, sequence[0]):\n        return ''.join(sequence_list[::-1])\n    else:\n        return ''.join(sequence_list)\n\ndef main():\n    while True:\n        n, m = map(int, input().split())\n        if n == 0 and m == 0:\n            break\n        glyph_dict = [parse_glyph(input()) for _ in range(n)]\n        monoliths = [parse_monolith(input()) for _ in range(m)]\n        for monolith in monoliths:\n            sequence = []\n            for row in monolith:\n                if any(row[i] == '*' for i in range(len(row))):\n                    sequence.append(row)\n                else:\n                    sequence.append(flip_bitmap(row) if is_flipped(glyph_dict, row) else row)\n            print(transliterate_sequence(glyph_dict, sequence))\n        print(\"#\")\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```\n\nThis script reads the input, processes the glyphs and monoliths, and outputs the transliterated sequences. It uses the provided functions to parse the glyphs and monoliths, identify the glyphs, and determine the direction of the sequence.",
