              "length": 651,
              "text": "To solve this problem, we need to follow the steps outlined in the problem statement. Here's a Python script that reads the input and outputs the transliteration of the sentences on the monoliths.\n\n```python\ndef read_glyph(glyph):\n    # Read the glyph details\n    c, h, w = map(int, input().split())\n    bitmap = [input() for _ in range(h)]\n    return c, bitmap\n\ndef read_string(string):\n    # Read the string details\n    h, w = map(int, input().split())\n    bitmap = [input() for _ in range(h)]\n    return bitmap\n\ndef find_glyph(bitmap, glyphs):\n    for c, g in glyphs:\n        if g == bitmap:\n            return c\n    return None\n\ndef find_flipped_glyph(bitmap, glyphs):\n    for c, g in glyphs:\n        if g[::-1] == bitmap:\n            return c\n    return None\n\ndef transliterate_string(string, glyphs):\n    # Determine if the string is written from right to left\n    from_right_to_left = False\n    for i in range(len(string)):\n        if find_flipped_glyph(string[i], glyphs) is not None:\n            from_right_to_left = True\n            break\n    \n    result = []\n    i = len(string) - 1 if from_right_to_left else 0\n    while i >= 0 if from_right_to_left else i < len(string):\n        if string[i] in [g[0] for g in glyphs]:\n            result.append(find_glyph(string[i], glyphs))\n        elif string[i] in [g[0] for g in glyphs][::-1]:\n            result.append(find_flipped_glyph(string[i], glyphs))\n        elif string[i][0] == '[':\n            # It's a box, so we need to transliterate the enclosed sequence\n            enclosed_sequence = []\n            j = i + 1\n            while string[j] != ']':\n                enclosed_sequence.append(string[j])\n                j += 1\n            enclosed_sequence = string[i + 1:j]\n            result.append('[' + transliterate_string(enclosed_sequence, glyphs) + ']')\n            i = j\n        else:\n            raise ValueError(\"Invalid character in string\")\n        i -= 1 if from_right_to_left else 1\n    \n    return ''.join(result[::-1]) if from_right_to_left else ''.join(result)\n\ndef main():\n    while True:\n        n, m = map(int, input().split())\n        if n == 0 and m == 0:\n            break\n        \n        glyphs = [read_glyph(input()) for _ in range(n)]\n        monoliths = [read_string(input()) for _ in range(m)]\n        \n        for string in monoliths:\n            print(transliterate_string(string, glyphs))\n        print('#')\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```\n\nThis script reads the input, processes each monolith, and outputs the transliteration of the sentence. It uses the provided glyphs to map the bitmap of each term in the sentence to the corresponding ASCII letter. The script also handles the case where a term might be a flipped glyph or a box enclosing another sequence.",
