              "text": "To solve this problem, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Read the input data.\n2. Process the glyph dictionary.\n3. Process each monolith.\n4. Transliterate the monolith based on the glyph dictionary and the rules provided.\n\nLet's start by writing the Python script to achieve this.\n\n```python\ndef read_glyph(glyph):\n    c, h, w = map(int, next(glyph).split())\n    bitmap = [next(glyph) for _ in range(h)]\n    return c, bitmap\n\ndef read_monolith(monolith):\n    h, w = map(int, next(monolith).split())\n    bitmap = [next(monolith) for _ in range(h)]\n    return bitmap\n\ndef find_glyph(bitmap, glyphs):\n    for c, g in glyphs:\n        if all(g[i][j] == bitmap[i][j] for i in range(len(g)) for j in range(len(g[0]))):\n            return c\n    return None\n\ndef find_flipped_glyph(bitmap, glyphs):\n    for c, g in glyphs:\n        flipped_g = [row[::-1] for row in g]\n        if all(flipped_g[i][j] == bitmap[i][j] for i in range(len(flipped_g)) for j in range(len(flipped_g[0]))):\n            return c\n    return None\n\ndef is_right_to_left(glyphs, monolith):\n    for i in range(len(monolith)):\n        if find_flipped_glyph(monolith[i], glyphs) is not None:\n            return True\n    return False\n\ndef transliterate_monolith(glyphs, monolith):\n    if is_right_to_left(glyphs, monolith):\n        return ''.join(find_flipped_glyph(row, glyphs) for row in reversed(monolith))\n    else:\n        return ''.join(find_glyph(row, glyphs) for row in monolith)\n\ndef process_dataset(glyphs, monoliths):\n    for monolith in monoliths:\n        monolith_bitmap = read_monolith(monolith)\n        transliterated = transliterate_monolith(glyphs, monolith_bitmap)\n        print(transliterated)\n    print('#')\n\nwhile True:\n    n, m = map(int, input().split())\n    if n == 0 and m == 0:\n        break\n    \n    glyphs = [read_glyph(input()) for _ in range(n)]\n    monoliths = [iter([input(), *read_monolith(input())]) for _ in range(m)]\n    \n    process_dataset(glyphs, monoliths)\n```\n\nThis script reads the input data, processes the glyph dictionary, and then processes each monolith to transliterate it based on the provided rules. The `read_glyph` function reads a glyph from the input, the `read_monolith` function reads a monolith from the input, and the `transliterate_monolith` function transliterates the monolith based on the glyph dictionary and the rules. The `is_right_to_left` function checks if the monolith should be transliterated from right to left. The `process_dataset` function processes a dataset and prints the transliterated sentences.",
