              "text": "To solve this problem, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Read and Parse Input**: \n   - Read the number of glyphs and the number of monoliths.\n   - Parse the glyph dictionary and the bitmaps for each glyph.\n   - Parse the bitmaps for each monolith.\n\n2. **Glyph Matching and Flipping**:\n   - Identify and match the glyphs in the monolith bitmaps.\n   - Determine if any glyphs need to be flipped.\n   - Determine the reading direction based on the flipping criteria.\n\n3. **Transliterate the Monoliths**:\n   - Transliterate the glyphs and rectangles into the corresponding characters.\n\n4. **Output the Results**:\n   - Print the transliterated sentences.\n   - Print `#` to separate datasets.\n\nLet's break down the solution with the corresponding Python code.\n\n### Step-by-Step Solution\n\n#### 1. Reading and Parsing Input\nWe will use a loop to read the input until we encounter `0 0`.\n\n```python\nwhile True:\n    n, m = map(int, input().split())\n    if n == 0 and m == 0:\n        break\n    \n    # Parse the glyph dictionary\n    glyphs = {}\n    for _ in range(n):\n        c, h, w = input().split()\n        h, w = int(h), int(w)\n        glyph = []\n        for _ in range(h):\n            row = input().strip()\n            glyph.append(row)\n        glyphs[c] = (glyph, h, w)\n    \n    # Parse the monoliths\n    monoliths = []\n    for _ in range(m):\n        h, w = map(int, input().split())\n        monolith = []\n        for _ in range(h):\n            row = input().strip()\n            monolith.append(row)\n        monoliths.append(monolith)\n```\n\n#### 2. Glyph Matching and Flipping\nWe need to match the glyphs in the monolith bitmaps and determine if they need to be flipped.\n\n```python\ndef match_and_flipping(monolith, glyphs, h, w):\n    flipped_glyphs = {c: (flip(glyph), h, w) for c, (glyph, h, w) in glyphs.items()}\n    glyphs.update(flipped_glyphs)\n    \n    result = []\n    for row in monolith:\n        for col in range(w):\n            for c, (glyph, gh, gw) in glyphs.items():\n                if is_subbitmap(glyph, row[col:col+gw], h):\n                    result.append(c)\n                    break\n    return result\n\ndef flip(glyph):\n    return [row[::-1] for row in glyph]\n\ndef is_subbitmap(target, source, h):\n    target_h, target_w = len(target), len(target[0])\n    if h < target_h:\n        return False\n    for i in range(h - target_h + 1):\n        if all(target[j] == source[i + j] for j in range(target_h)):\n            return True\n    return False\n```\n\n#### 3. Transliterate the Monoliths\nWe need to determine the reading direction and then transliterate.\n\n```python\ndef determine_reading_direction(result):\n    for i in range(len(result)):\n        if result[i] not in glyphs and result[i].swapcase() in glyphs:\n            return True\n    return False\n\ndef transliterate(monolith):\n    result = match_and_flipping(monolith, glyphs, len(monolith), len(monolith[0]))\n    if determine_reading_direction(result):\n        return ''.join(result[::-1])\n    else:\n        return ''.join(result)\n\n# Transliterate each monolith\nfor monolith in monoliths:\n    print(transliterate(monolith))\n```\n\n#### 4. Output the Results\nPrint the results and separate datasets.\n\n```python\nprint(\"#\")\n```\n\n### Complete Code\n\n```python\ndef match_and_flipping(monolith, glyphs, h, w):\n    flipped_glyphs = {c: (flip(glyph), h, w) for c, (glyph, h, w) in glyphs.items()}\n    glyphs.update(flipped_glyphs)\n    \n    result = []\n    for row in monolith:\n        for col in range(w):\n            for c, (glyph, gh, gw) in glyphs.items():\n                if is_subbitmap(glyph, row[col:col+gw], h):\n                    result.append(c)\n                    break\n    return result\n\ndef flip(glyph):\n    return [row[::-1] for row in glyph]\n\ndef is_subbitmap(target, source, h):\n    target_h, target_w = len(target), len(target[0])\n    if h < target_h:\n        return False\n    for i in range(h - target_h + 1):\n        if all(target[j] == source[i + j] for j in range(target_h)):\n            return True\n    return False\n\ndef determine_reading_direction(result):\n    for i in range(len(result)):\n        if result[i] not in glyphs and result[i].swapcase() in glyphs:\n            return True\n    return False\n\ndef transliterate(monolith):\n    result = match_and_flipping(monolith, glyphs, len(monolith), len(monolith[0]))\n    if determine_reading_direction(result):\n        return ''.join(result[::-1])\n    else:\n        return ''.join(result)\n\nwhile True:\n    n, m = map(int, input().split())\n    if n == 0 and m == 0:\n        break\n    \n    glyphs = {}\n    for _ in range(n):\n        c, h, w = input().split()\n        h, w = int(h), int(w)\n        glyph = []\n        for _ in range(h):\n            row = input().strip()\n            glyph.append(row)\n        glyphs[c] = (glyph, h, w)\n    \n    monoliths = []\n    for _ in range(m):\n        h, w = map(int, input().split())\n        monolith = []\n        for _ in range(h):\n            row = input().strip()\n            monolith.append(row)\n        monoliths.append(monolith)\n    \n    for monolith in monoliths:\n        print(transliterate(monolith))\n    print(\"#\")\n```\n\nThis code reads the input, processes each monolith, and outputs the transliterated sentences.",
