              "text": "To solve this problem, we need to count the number of ways to split the string \\( t \\) such that each part is included in the set \\( S \\). We can use dynamic programming to achieve this.\n\nHere's the step-by-step plan:\n1. Read the input values for \\( N \\), the set \\( S \\), and the string \\( t \\).\n2. Use a dynamic programming array \\( dp \\) where \\( dp[i] \\) represents the number of ways to split the first \\( i \\) characters of \\( t \\).\n3. Initialize \\( dp[0] = 1 \\) because there's one way to split an empty string (doing nothing).\n4. Iterate through each character of \\( t \\) and for each character, check all substrings of \\( S \\) that match the suffix of \\( t \\) starting from the current character.\n5. Update the \\( dp \\) array based on the matches.\n6. Finally, print the result modulo \\( 1,000,000,007 \\).\n\nLet's implement this in Python:\n\n```python\ndef count_ways_to_split(N, S, t):\n    MOD = 1000000007\n    \n    # Convert set S to a list for easier manipulation\n    S = list(S)\n    \n    # Initialize dp array\n    dp = [0] * (len(t) + 1)\n    dp[0] = 1\n    \n    # Iterate through each character of t\n    for i in range(1, len(t) + 1):\n        for s in S:\n            # Check if the suffix of t matches any string in S\n            if t[i - len(s):i] == s:\n                dp[i] += dp[i - len(s)]\n                dp[i] %= MOD\n    \n    return dp[len(t)]\n\n# Read input\nN = int(input())\nS = set()\nfor _ in range(N):\n    S.add(input().strip())\nt = input().strip()\n\n# Calculate and print the result\nresult = count_ways_to_split(N, S, t)\nprint(result)\n```\n\nThis script reads the input, processes the set \\( S \\), and uses dynamic programming to count the number of ways to split the string \\( t \\). The result is then printed modulo \\( 1,000,000,007 \\).",
