              "length": 503,
              "text": "To solve this problem, we need to count the number of valid subsequences \"JOI\" and \"IOI\" that can be formed from the given string `S`. The key is to count the occurrences of each character and then use these counts to determine the maximum number of mini JOIOI towers that can be built.\n\nHere's the Python script to solve the problem:\n\n```python\n# Read input\nN = int(input())\nS = input()\n\n# Initialize counters for J, O, and I\nJ_count = 0\nO_count = 0\nI_count = 0\n\n# Count the occurrences of each character\nfor char in S:\n    if char == 'J':\n        J_count += 1\n    elif char == 'O':\n        O_count += 1\n    elif char == 'I':\n        I_count += 1\n\n# Calculate the maximum number of mini JOIOI towers\n# We can build a mini JOIOI tower if we have at least one \"JOI\" and one \"IOI\"\n# The number of \"JOI\" is limited by the minimum of J_count, O_count, and I_count - 1\nJOI_count = min(J_count, O_count, I_count - 1)\n# The number of \"IOI\" is limited by the minimum of O_count, I_count, and J_count - 1\nIOI_count = min(O_count, I_count, J_count - 1)\n\n# The maximum number of mini JOIOI towers is the minimum of JOI_count and IOI_count\nmax_towers = min(JOI_count, IOI_count)\n\n# Output the result\nprint(max_towers)\n```\n\nLet's break down the logic:\n1. We read the input and count the occurrences of 'J', 'O', and 'I'.\n2. We calculate the number of valid \"JOI\" and \"IOI\" subsequences.\n3. The number of \"JOI\" is limited by the minimum of `J_count`, `O_count`, and `I_count - 1`.\n4. The number of \"IOI\" is limited by the minimum of `O_count`, `I_count`, and `J_count - 1`.\n5. The maximum number of mini JOIOI towers is the minimum of the counts of \"JOI\" and \"IOI\".\n\nThis script will correctly handle the given examples and any other input within the specified constraints.",
