              "text": "To solve this problem, we need to count the maximum number of mini JOIOI towers that can be built using the given disks. A mini JOIOI tower consists of three disks that can be read as \"JOI\" or \"IOI\" in ascending order of diameter. Here is the Python script to achieve this:\n\n```python\n# Read the input\nN = int(input())\nS = input()\n\n# Initialize counters for JOI and IOI subsequences\ncount_JOI = 0\ncount_IOI = 0\n\n# Iterate through the string to count JOI and IOI subsequences\nfor i in range(N - 2):\n    if S[i] == 'J' and S[i + 1] == 'O' and S[i + 2] == 'I':\n        count_JOI += 1\n    if S[i] == 'I' and S[i + 1] == 'O' and S[i + 2] == 'I':\n        count_IOI += 1\n\n# The maximum number of mini JOIOI towers is the minimum of count_JOI and count_IOI\nmax_towers = min(count_JOI, count_IOI)\n\n# Output the result\nprint(max_towers)\n```\n\nThis script reads the input, iterates through the string to count the occurrences of \"JOI\" and \"IOI\" subsequences, and then outputs the minimum of these counts as the maximum number of mini JOIOI towers that can be built.",
