              "text": "To solve this problem, we need to count the maximum number of mini JOIOI towers that can be built using the given disks. A mini JOIOI tower consists of three disks that can be read as JOI or IOI in ascending order of diameter. We can use dynamic programming to keep track of the counts of JOI and IOI subsequences.\n\nHere's the Python script to solve the problem:\n\n```python\n# Read input\nN = int(input())\nS = input()\n\n# Initialize counters for JOI and IOI subsequences\njo_count = 0\nio_count = 0\njoi_count = 0\n\n# Iterate through the string\nfor char in S:\n    if char == 'J':\n        # Reset jo_count and update joi_count\n        jo_count = 0\n        joi_count = max(joi_count, io_count)\n    elif char == 'O':\n        # Update jo_count and joi_count\n        jo_count += 1\n        joi_count = max(joi_count, io_count + jo_count)\n    elif char == 'I':\n        # Update io_count and joi_count\n        io_count += 1\n        joi_count = max(joi_count, io_count)\n    else:\n        # Invalid character\n        print(\"Invalid character in input string\")\n        break\n\n# The maximum number of mini JOIOI towers is the value of joi_count\nprint(joi_count)\n```\n\nThis script reads the input string and iterates through each character, updating the counters for JOI and IOI subsequences. It uses dynamic programming to keep track of the maximum number of mini JOIOI towers that can be built. The final result is printed to the standard output.",
