              "text": "To solve the problem, we need to understand the concept of Hamming Distance. The Hamming Distance between two strings of equal length is the number of positions at which the corresponding symbols are different. \n\nGiven the constraints, the problem can be simplified by understanding that the maximum Hamming Distance between the original string and any permutation of it can be achieved when no character in the permutation is in its original position. This scenario corresponds to the permutations where each character is swapped with another character in such a way that no character remains in its original position.\n\nFor a string of length \\(L\\) with \\(L\\) distinct characters, the maximum Hamming Distance is \\(L\\). This is only possible if every character is moved to a different position, which is a derangement of the string.\n\nThe number of derangements \\(D(n)\\) of \\(n\\) items can be calculated using the formula:\n\\[ D(n) = n! \\sum_{i=0}^{n} \\frac{(-1)^i}{i!} \\]\n\nGiven the constraints, \\(L\\) can be at most 94, and the factorial and sum can be quite large, so we need to calculate the derangement modulo \\(1000000007\\).\n\nHere is the Python script to solve the problem:\n\n```python\ndef factorial(n):\n    if n == 0 or n == 1:\n        return 1\n    return n * factorial(n - 1)\n\ndef derangement(n):\n    derange = 0\n    for i in range(n + 1):\n        derange += (-1)**i / factorial(i)\n    return int(round(derange * factorial(n)))\n\ndef main():\n    L = int(input())\n    _ = input()  # Read the string, we don't need it for the calculation\n    \n    mod = 1000000007\n    print(derangement(L) % mod)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```\n\nExplanation:\n1. **factorial(n)**: A recursive function to compute the factorial of a number.\n2. **derangement(n)**: This function computes the derangement using the formula provided. It uses a loop to compute the sum part of the derangement formula and then multiplies it by the factorial of \\(n\\). The result is rounded and converted to an integer.\n3. **main()**: This function reads the input, discards the string, and calculates the derangement of the given length \\(L\\). The result is printed modulo \\(1000000007\\).\n\nThis script efficiently computes the required number of permutations for the given constraints.",
